si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Description", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Trouble diagnoses indicate work procedures required to diagnose problems effectively. Observe the following instructions before diagnosing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Before performing trouble diagnoses, read the “Work Flow” in each section.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "After repairs, re-check that the problem has been completely eliminated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Refer to Component Parts and Harness Connector Location for the Systems described in each section for identification/location of components and harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "When checking circuit continuity, ignition switch should be OFF.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Refer to the Circuit Diagram for quick pinpoint check.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "If you need to check circuit continuity between harness connectors in more detail, such as when a sub-harness is used, refer to Wiring Diagram in each individual section and Harness Layout in PG section for identification of harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "Before checking voltage at connectors, check battery voltage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002000ENG.html", "After accomplishing the Diagnosis Procedures and Electrical Components Inspection, check that all harness connectors are reconnected as they were.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "How to Follow Test Groups in Trouble Diagnosis", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Test group number and test group title", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Test group number and test group title are shown in the upper portion of each test group.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Work and diagnosis procedure", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Start to diagnose a problem using procedures indicated in enclosed test groups.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Questions and results", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Questions and required results are indicated in test group.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Action", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102U0000E00ENG.html", "Next action for each test group is indicated based on result of each question.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010380000E00ENG.html", "Key to Symbols Signifying Measurements or Procedures", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011190000E00ENG.html", "HOW TO READ CONFIGURATION DIAGRAMS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011190000E00ENG.html", "The wiring harness diagrams clearly show the connector locations and harness routings at each site on actual vehicles.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011200000K00ENG.html", "HOW TO READ CIRCUIT DIAGRAMS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011200000K00ENG.html", "The circuit of each system from the fuse (or fusible link) to earth is shown. The power source is shown at the top and the earth at the bottom to facilitate understanding of how the current flows.The circuit diagrams show the state when switches are not operated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011200000K00ENG.html", "Connector symbols are listed at the end of each system circuit diagram.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "CONNECTOR SYMBOLS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "There are many connectors and earth in the circuit, however when they are shown in the circuit diagram, the representation method is determined as shown below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "No.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Connector/Grounding", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Symbol", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Contents", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Connector connection marking", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "–", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "The male and female terminals are indicated as shown. The connector with male terminal(s) is called as male connector and indicated by two connector contour lines, while the connector with female terminal(s) is called as female connector and indicated by single connector contour line.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Connector symbol marking", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "1", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Each symbol represents view of the actual vehicle\'s connector seen from the direction shown in the figure. As for the connection point with the device, the device side connector symbol is shown. As for the intermediate connector, both male side connector symbol or female side connector symbol is shown. As for option connectors, spare connectors and check connectors, no device is connected, and so the harness-side connector symbol is shown for these connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "However, method for showing symbol for the data link connector differs from above.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "2", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "3", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "4", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Connection between a device and the harness is either by direct insertion in the device (direct connection type) or by connection with a harness connector furnished on the device side (harness connection type). The two types are indicated as illustrated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "5", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "6", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Ground marking", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "7", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "Grounding is either by body ground, device earth or control unit interior ground. These are indicated as illustrated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "8", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101B0001500ENG.html", "9", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "WIRE COLOR CODES", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "Wire colors are indicated by alphabet and color and as follows.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "&lt;Copper wire>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "&lt;Aluminum wire>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "If a cable has two colors, the first of the two color code characters indicates the basic color (color of the cable coating) and the second indicates the marking color.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "No.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "Meaning", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "1", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "&lt;F>: Flexible wire", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "&lt;T>: Twisted wire", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "2", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "Wire size (mm2)*", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "3", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "Basic color (color of the cable coating)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "4", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "Marking color", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011810000100ENG.html", "*: No code indicates 0.5 mm2. Cable color code in parentheses indicates 0.3 mm2.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "How to Repair Aluminum Wires", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS FOR THE HANDLING OF ALUMINUM WIRES", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "If an aluminum wire is damaged (e.g. broken), never perform the repair method for copper wires (soldering).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Never perform electrotap for connecting broken aluminum wires.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "To secure the wire fixing strength (a force to protect aluminum wire from being disconnected from crimp terminal) and electrical conductivity, always use the dedicated harness repair kit and caulking tool [SST: KV99112600] when repairing broken wires.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "HOW TO DISTINGUISH ALUMINUM WIRES", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Wiring color: Lavender (Color code: LA)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "HOW TO REPAIR BROKEN WIRES", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Insert heat shrinkable tube  into the target aluminum wire  beforehand.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Strip wire terminal approximately 10 mm and insert it into crimp terminal .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Check wire size and use appropriate crimp terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Set crimp terminal to the die (tooth) of caulking tool [SST: KV99112600].", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Use appropriate die (tooth) of caulking tool [SST: KV99112600] according to the crimp terminal size.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Apply load until the handle of caulking tool [SST: KV99112600] is released.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "The handle of the specified caulking tool [SST: KV99112600] is not opened until crimping is completed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "After crimping both sides, pull wire at both ends to check that they are not disconnected from crimp terminals.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Cover the crimp terminal with heat shrinkable tube  and heat the tube with industrial dryer .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "After heating heat shrinkable tube , check that adhesive  is squeezed out from both ends of tube to the entire perimeter.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "Wind insulating tape  around heat shrinkable tube for the purpose of waterproof and anticorrosion.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "HOW TO EXTEND WIRES", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010840000B00ENG.html", "When repairing a broken aluminum wire, it can be extended by connecting aluminum wire  with copper wire  by using crimp terminal .", "ptxt");
