si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104O0000E00ENG.html", "Use tightening torque with lubricant for the new standard bolts/nuts in principle. Friction coefficient stabilizer is applied to the new standard bolts/nuts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104O0000E00ENG.html", "However, use tightening torque without lubricant for the following cases. Friction coefficient stabilizer is not applied to the following bolts/nuts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104O0000E00ENG.html", "Grade 4.8, M6 size bolt, Conical spring washer installed", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104O0000E00ENG.html", "Paint removing nut (Size M6 and M8) for fixing with weld bolt", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104O0000E00ENG.html", "DISCRIMINATION OF BOLTS AND NUTS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS FOR SUPPLEMENTAL RESTRAINT SYSTEM (SRS) AIR BAG AND SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER : Precautions", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "The Supplemental Restraint System such as “AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER”, used along with a front seat belt, helps to reduce the risk or severity of injury to the driver and front passenger for certain types of collision.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "Information necessary to service the system safely is included in the “SRS AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT” of this Service Manual.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "Always observe the following items for preventing accidental activation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "To avoid rendering the SRS inoperative, which could increase the risk of personal injury or death in the event of a collision that would result in air bag inflation, it is recommended that all maintenance and repair be performed by an authorized Mitsubishi Motors dealer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "Improper repair, including incorrect removal and installation of the SRS, can lead to personal injury caused by unintentional activation of the system. For removal of Spiral Cable and Air Bag Module, see “SRS AIR BAG”.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "Never use electrical test equipment on any circuit related to the SRS unless instructed to in this Service Manual. SRS wiring harnesses can be identified by yellow harnesses or harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS WHEN USING POWER TOOLS (AIR OR ELECTRIC) AND HAMMERS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "When working near the Air Bag Diagnosis Sensor Unit or other Air Bag System sensors with the ignition/power switch ON or engine running, never use air or electric power tools or strike near the sensor(s) with a hammer. Heavy vibration could activate the sensor(s) and deploy the air bag(s), possibly causing serious injury.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103Z0000J00ENG.html", "When using air or electric power tools or hammers, always switch the ignition/power switch OFF, disconnect the 12V battery or batteries, and wait at least 3 minutes before performing any service.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010850000B00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS FOR PROCEDURE WITHOUT COWL TOP COVER : Precautions", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010850000B00ENG.html", "When performing the procedure after removing cowl top cover, cover the lower end of windshield with urethane, etc to prevent damage to windshield.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Precautions for Removing Battery Terminal", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "With the adoption of Auto ACC function, ACC power is automatically supplied by operating the Keyless operation key or remote keyless entry or by opening/closing the driver side door. In addition, ACC power is supplied even after the ignition switch is turned to the OFF position, i.e. ACC power is supplied for a certain fixed time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "When disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, turn off the ACC power before disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, observing “How to disconnect 12V battery terminal” described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Some ECUs operate for a certain fixed time even after ignition switch is turned OFF and ignition power supply is stopped. If the battery terminal is disconnected before ECU stops, accidental DTC detection or ECU data damage may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "For vehicles with the 2-batteries, be sure to connect the main battery and the sub battery before turning ON the ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "If the ignition switch is turned ON with any one of the terminals of main battery and sub battery disconnected, then DTC may be detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "After installing the 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "The removal of 12V battery may cause a DTC detection error.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "HOW TO DISCONNECT 12V BATTERY TERMINAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Disconnect 12V battery terminal according to instruction described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Open the hood.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the OFF position with the driver side door opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Get out of the vehicle and close the driver side door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "While waiting, never operate the vehicle such as locking, opening, and closing doors. Violation of this caution results in the activation of ACC power supply according to the Auto ACC function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "Remove 12V battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010860000E00ENG.html", "After installing 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002200ENG.html", "Description", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010101J0002200ENG.html", "Observe the following precautions to ensure safe and proper servicing. These precautions are not described in each individual section.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "General Precautions", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Do not operate the engine for an extended period of time without proper exhaust ventilation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Keep the work area well ventilated and free of any inflammable materials. Special care should be taken when handling any inflammable or poisonous materials, such as gasoline, refrigerant gas, etc. When working in a pit or other enclosed area, be sure to properly ventilate the area before working with hazardous materials.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Do not smoke while working on the vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Before jacking up the vehicle, apply wheel chocks or other tire blocks to the wheels to prevent the vehicle from moving. After jacking up the vehicle, support the vehicle weight with safety stands at the points designated for proper lifting before working on the vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "These operations should be done on a level surface.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "When removing a heavy component such as the engine or transaxle/transmission, be careful not to lose your balance and drop them. Also, do not allow them to strike adjacent parts, especially the brake tubes and master cylinder.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Before starting repairs which do not require battery power:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Turn off ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Disconnect the negative battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "If the battery terminals are disconnected, recorded memory of radio and each control unit is erased.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "For vehicles with two batteries, be sure to remove both batteries when instructed to remove 12V battery in the service manual. If specified as main battery or sub battery, then do as instructed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "To prevent serious burns:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Avoid contact with hot metal parts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Do not remove the radiator cap when the engine is hot.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Dispose of drained oil or the solvent used for cleaning parts in an appropriate manner.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Do not attempt to top off the fuel tank after the fuel pump nozzle shuts off automatically.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Continued refueling may cause fuel overflow, resulting in fuel spray and possibly a fire.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Clean all disassembled parts in the designated liquid or solvent prior to inspection or assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Replace oil seals, gaskets, packings, O-rings, locking washers, cotter pins, self-locking nuts, etc. with new ones.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Replace inner and outer races of tapered roller bearings and needle bearings as a set.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Arrange the disassembled parts in accordance with their assembled locations and sequence.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Do not touch the terminals of electrical components which use microcomputers (such as ECM).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Static electricity may damage internal electronic components.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "After disconnecting vacuum or air hoses, attach a tag to indicate the proper connection.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Use only the fluids and lubricants specified in this manual.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Use approved bonding agent, sealants or their equivalents when required.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Use hand tools, power tools (disassembly only) and recommended special tools where specified for safe and efficient service repairs.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "When repairing the fuel, oil, water, vacuum or exhaust systems, check all affected lines for leakage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Before servicing the vehicle:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Protect fenders, upholstery and carpeting with appropriate covers.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "Take caution that keys, buckles or buttons do not scratch paint.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102J0000E00ENG.html", "To prevent ECM from storing the diagnostic trouble codes, never carelessly disconnect the harness connectors which are related to the engine control system and TCM (transmission control module) system. The connectors should be disconnected only when working according to the WORK FLOW of TROUBLE DIAGNOSES in EC and TM sections.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "Three Way Catalyst", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "If a large amount of unburned fuel flows into the catalyst, the catalyst temperature will be excessively high. To prevent this, follow the instructions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "Use unleaded gasoline only. Leaded gasoline will seriously damage the three way catalyst.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "When checking for ignition spark or measuring engine compression, make tests quickly and only when necessary.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "Do not run engine when the fuel tank level is low, otherwise the engine may misfire, causing damage to the catalyst.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104M0000E00ENG.html", "Do not place the vehicle on flammable material. Keep flammable material off the exhaust pipe and the three way catalyst.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Multiport Fuel Injection System or Engine Control System", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Before connecting or disconnecting any harness connector for the multiport fuel injection system or ECM:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to “OFF” position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Disconnect negative battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Otherwise, there may be damage to ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Before disconnecting pressurized fuel line from fuel pump to injectors, be sure to release fuel pressure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010103E0000E00ENG.html", "Be careful not to jar components such as ECM and mass air flow sensor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "Hoses", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "HOSE REMOVAL AND INSTALLATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "To prevent damage to rubber hose, do not pry off rubber hose with tapered tool or screwdriver.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "To reinstall the rubber hose securely, check that hose insertion length and orientation is correct. (If tube is equipped with hose stopper, insert rubber hose into tube until it butts up against hose stopper.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "HOSE CLAMPING", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "If old rubber hose is re-used, install hose clamp in its original position (at the indentation where the old clamp was). If there is a trace of tube bulging left on the old rubber hose, align rubber hose at that position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "Discard old clamps; replace with new ones.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102R0000E00ENG.html", "After installing plate clamps, apply force to them in the direction of the arrow, tightening rubber hose equally all around.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Engine Oils", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Prolonged and repeated contact with used engine oil may cause skin cancer. Try to avoid direct skin contact with used oil.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "If skin contact is made, wash thoroughly with soap or hand cleaner as soon as possible.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "HEALTH PROTECTION PRECAUTIONS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Avoid prolonged and repeated contact with oils, particularly used engine oils.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Wear protective clothing, including impervious gloves where practicable.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Do not put oily rags in pockets.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Avoid contaminating clothes, particularly underpants, with oil.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Heavily soiled clothing and oil-impregnated footwear should not be worn. Overalls must be cleaned regularly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "First aid treatment should be obtained immediately for open cuts and wounds.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Use barrier creams, applying them before each work period, to help the removal of oil from the skin.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Wash with soap and water to ensure all oil is removed (skin cleansers and nail brushes will help). Preparations containing lanolin replace the natural skin oils which have been removed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Do not use gasoline, kerosene, diesel fuel, gas oil, thinners or solvents for cleaning skin.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "If skin disorders develop, obtain medical advice without delay.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Where practical, degrease components prior to handling.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Where there is a risk of eye contact, eye protection should be worn, for example, chemical goggles or face shields; in addition an eye wash facility should be provided.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION PRECAUTIONS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "Dispose of used oil and used oil filters through authorized waste disposal contractors to licensed waste disposal sites, or to the waste oil reclamation trade. If in doubt, contact the local authority for advice on disposal facilities.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "It is illegal to pour used oil on to the ground, down sewers or drains, or into water sources.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010220000E00ENG.html", "The regulations concerning pollution vary between regions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010100P0000E00ENG.html", "Air Conditioning", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010100P0000E00ENG.html", "Use an approved refrigerant recovery unit any time the air conditioning system must be discharged. Refer to HA section “REFRIGERATION SYSTEM” for specific instructions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Fuel", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Use unleaded regular gasoline with an octane rating of at last 87 AKI (Anti-Knock Index) number (Research octane number 91).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Using a fuel other than that specified could adversely affect the emission control system, and may also affect warranty coverage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Under no circumstances should a leaded gasoline be used, because this will damage the three-way catalyst.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Do not use E-15 or E-85 fuel in the vehicle. The vehicle is not designed to run on E-15 or E-85 fuel. Using E-15 or E-85 fuel in a vehicle not specifically designed for E-15 or E-85 fuel can adversely affect the emission control devices and systems of the vehicle. Damage caused by such fuel is not covered by the Mitsubishi Motors new vehicle limited warranty.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010102D0000E00ENG.html", "Do not use fuel that contains the octane booster methylcyclopentadienyl manganese tricarbonyl (MMT). Using fuel containing MMT may adversely affect vehicle performance and vehicle emissions. Not all fuel dispensers are labeled to indicate MMT content, so you may have to consult your petrol retailer for more details. Note that Federal and California laws prohibit the use of MMT in reformulated gasoline.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "PRE-INSPECTION CONDITION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "\"Pre-inspection condition\" refers to the condition that the vehicle must be in before proper engine inspection can be carried out. If you see the words \"Set the vehicle to the pre-inspection condition\". in this manual, it means to set the vehicle to the following condition.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "Engine coolant temperature: 80 - 90°C (176 - 194°F)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "Lights, electric cooling fan and all accessories: OFF", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "CVT: P range", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010910000500ENG.html", "On vehicles for Canada, the headlight, taillight, etc. remain lit even when the lighting switch is in \"OFF\" position but this is no problem for checks.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "VEHICLE WASHING", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "If high-pressure car-washing equipment or steam car-washing equipment is used to wash the vehicle, be sure to note the following information in order to avoid damage to plastic components, etc.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "Spray nozzle distance: Approx. 70 cm or more", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "Spray pressure: 8,000 kPa or less", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "Spray temperature: 82°C or less", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010950000500ENG.html", "Time of concentrated spray to one point: within 30 sec.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS FOR INSTALLATION OF ON-VEHICLE RADIO TRANSMISSION EQUIPMENT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "The computers (control unit) for various on-vehicle electronic equipment are provided with sufficient protective measures against external radio wave interference. However, because the on-vehicle radio transmission equipment may affect adversely the computers (control unit), pay attention to the following precautions for installation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Install radio transmission equipment and antenna (including coaxial cables) 200 mm or more away from the computers (control unit) for on-vehicle electronic equipment.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Because radio wave is radiated from the coaxial cables of the antenna for radio transmission equipment, do not route the cables in parallel with the vehicle wiring harness.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Install only radio transmission equipment with the frequencies, output, and radio wave types described in the table.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "FREQUENCY, OUTPUT, AND RADIO WAVE TYPE OF THE RADIO TRANSMISSION EQUIPMENT", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Frequency (MHz)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Maximum output power (W)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "3.5", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "50", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "7", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "14", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "21", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "26-30", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "50-54", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "144-174", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "380-410", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "30", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "430", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "1,260", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "10", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011130000700ENG.html", "Install the antenna for radio transmission equipment only to the position shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010960000500ENG.html", "BOLTS AND NUTS WITH STABILIZER FOR COEFFICIENT OF FRICTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010960000500ENG.html", "The bolts and nuts with stabilizer for coefficient of friction have been used for the connections such as the suspension arm and crossmember in order to stabilize the axial force and to ensure the high axial force at bolt/nut connections, resulting in improved reliability.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010960000500ENG.html", "The bolts and nuts with stabilizer for coefficient of friction mean that the bolts and nuts with surface treatment to stabilize and reduce the coefficient of friction, allowing to achieve the stable axial force and to secure the high axial force with low tightening torque.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "THE TIGHTENING TORQUE WHEN AN EXTENSION TOOL IS USED", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "When using an extension tool, calculate the torque value (T\') by the formula below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "If tightened until the read value of the torque wrench reaches the specified torque (T), the actual tightening torque will be excessive.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "Make sure that the torque wrench and the extension tool are connected to each other in a straight line when using them. If they are not connected in a straight line, the tightening torque does not satisfy the specified value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "Formula T\'=T×L2/(L1+L2)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "Symbol", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "T\'", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "The read value of the torque wrench (N·m)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "T", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "The specified tightening torque (N·m)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "L1", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "The length of the extension tool (mm)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "L2", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501010970000500ENG.html", "The length of the torque wrench (mm)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011110000500ENG.html", "APPLICATION OF ANTI-CORROSION AGENTS AND UNDERCOATS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011110000500ENG.html", "If oil or grease gets onto the oxygen sensor, it will cause a drop in the performance of the sensor. Cover the oxygen sensor with a protective cover when applying anti-corrosion agents and undercoats.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "SUPPORT LOCATIONS FOR LIFTING AND JACKING", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "SUPPORT POSITIONS FOR A GARAGE JACK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "Be sure to support the specified locations only. Otherwise, deformation of vehicle may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "Be careful to avoid damage to the front under cover or rear differential carrier assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "SUPPORT POSITIONS FOR RIGID RACKS, SINGLE-POST LIFT OR DOUBLE-POST LIFT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "If rubber attachments with grooves that are too thick are used at the front support positions, the front fender may become bent, so be sure to use rubber attachments with groove thicknesses of 18 mm or less.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "If attachments which are not high enough are used, they may damage areas such as the side step. Be sure to use attachments which are high enough, or remove the side step if not using attachments.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "PLATE TYPE LIFT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "Be careful to avoid damage to the side sill garnish.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N501011070000500ENG.html", "Support the notch with a spacer (100-mm width, 100 mm height and 200-mm depth).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "Tow Truck Towing", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "To avoid the risk of minor injury or property damage : If the 12V battery has low or no voltage, the transmission cannot be shifted into neutral. To transport the vehicle, it must have all four wheels off the ground and placed on a flatbed or track system.", "par1");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "All applicable state or Provincial laws and local laws regarding the towing operation must be obeyed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "It is necessary to use proper towing equipment to avoid possible damage to the vehicle during towing operation. Towing is in accordance with Towing Procedure Manual at dealer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "Always attach safety chains before towing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "When towing the front wheels on towing dollies:", "par2");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104P0000E00ENG.html", "Ignition switch off, and secure the steering wheel in a straight ahead with a rope or similar device.", "par3");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "Vehicle Recovery (Freeing a Stuck Vehicle)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "Do not pull a stuck vehicle that has a 12V battery that has low or no voltage. If the 12V battery has low or no voltage, the transmission cannot be shifted into neutral.", "par4");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "There are not has hooks for towing, tie down (shipping etc.) as Mitsubishi Motors genuine parts.", "par1");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "Never tow another vehicle.", "par2");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "Never be towed vehicle.", "par5");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5010104U0000E00ENG.html", "If vehicle face to stuck etc., contact a professional towing service to recovery the vehicle.", "par3");
