si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "Description", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "ECM input/output valve when the engine control system operates normally.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "The SP value can be confirmed in Data List items whose name ends with \"SP MIN\" and \"SP MAX\" like the following example.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "(Example)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "SP value(MAX): Base fuel schedule (SP MAX)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "SP value(MIN): Base fuel schedule (SP MIN)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "When the indicated value of \"DATA MONITOR\" mode is within the SP value, the engine control system is confirmed OK. When the indicated value of \"DATA MONITOR\" mode is not within the SP value, the engine control system may have one or more malfunctions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "The SP value will be displayed for the following three items:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "Base fuel schedule (The fuel injection pulse width programmed into ECM prior to any learned on board correction)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "Air fuel ratio compensation B1 (The mean value of air-fuel ratio feedback correction factor per cycle)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020401G0007I00ENG.html", "Mass air flow sensor B1 (The signal frequency of the mass air flow sensor)", "ptxt");
