si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Precautions for Removing Battery Terminal", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "With the adoption of Auto ACC function, ACC power is automatically supplied by operating the Keyless operation key or remote keyless entry or by opening/closing the driver side door. In addition, ACC power is supplied even after the ignition switch is turned to the OFF position, i.e. ACC power is supplied for a certain fixed time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "When disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, turn off the ACC power before disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, observing “How to disconnect 12V battery terminal” described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Some ECUs operate for a certain fixed time even after ignition switch is turned OFF and ignition power supply is stopped. If the battery terminal is disconnected before ECU stops, accidental DTC detection or ECU data damage may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "For vehicles with the 2-batteries, be sure to connect the main battery and the sub battery before turning ON the ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "If the ignition switch is turned ON with any one of the terminals of main battery and sub battery disconnected, then DTC may be detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "After installing the 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "The removal of 12V battery may cause a DTC detection error.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "HOW TO DISCONNECT 12V BATTERY TERMINAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Disconnect 12V battery terminal according to instruction described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Open the hood.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the OFF position with the driver side door opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Get out of the vehicle and close the driver side door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "While waiting, never operate the vehicle such as locking, opening, and closing doors. Violation of this caution results in the activation of ACC power supply according to the Auto ACC function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802R0000J00ENG.html", "Remove 12V battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "Precaution for Supplemental Restraint System (SRS) \"AIR BAG\" and \"SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER\"", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "The Supplemental Restraint System such as “AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER”, used along with a front seat belt, helps to reduce the risk or severity of injury to the driver and front passenger for certain types of collision.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "Information necessary to service the system safely is included in the “SRS AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT” of this Service Manual.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "Always observe the following items for preventing accidental activation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "To avoid rendering the SRS inoperative, which could increase the risk of personal injury or death in the event of a collision that would result in air bag inflation, it is recommended that all maintenance and repair be performed by an authorized Mitsubishi Motors dealer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "Improper repair, including incorrect removal and installation of the SRS, can lead to personal injury caused by unintentional activation of the system. For removal of Spiral Cable and Air Bag Module, see “SRS AIR BAG”.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "Never use electrical test equipment on any circuit related to the SRS unless instructed to in this Service Manual. SRS wiring harnesses can be identified by yellow harnesses or harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS WHEN USING POWER TOOLS (AIR OR ELECTRIC) AND HAMMERS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "When working near the Air Bag Diagnosis Sensor Unit or other Air Bag System sensors with the ignition/power switch ON or engine running, never use air or electric power tools or strike near the sensor(s) with a hammer. Heavy vibration could activate the sensor(s) and deploy the air bag(s), possibly causing serious injury.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020803I0000H00ENG.html", "When using air or electric power tools or hammers, always switch the ignition/power switch OFF, disconnect the 12V battery or batteries, and wait at least 3 minutes before performing any service.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801M0000J00ENG.html", "Exploded View", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801M0000J00ENG.html", "Accelerator pedal assembly", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801M0000J00ENG.html", "Brake pedal assembly", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801M0000J00ENG.html", ": N·m (kg-m, in-lb)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Removal and Installation", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "REMOVAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Never disassemble accelerator pedal assembly. Never remove accelerator pedal position sensor from accelerator pedal assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Avoid impact from dropping etc. during handling.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Be careful to keep accelerator pedal assembly away from water.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Loosen mounting bolts, and remove accelerator pedal assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Disconnect accelerator pedal position sensor harness connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "INSTALLATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Note the following, and install in the reverse order of removal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Install the protrusion  of the bracket into the locating hole  of the accelerator pedal assembly before tightening the accelerator pedal assembly mounting bolts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", ": Locating pin", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "When inserting accelerator pedal assembly to protrusion , never scratch locating hole  with the protrusion.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "Tighten bolts with the locating pin securely inserted in the bracket hole.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020802U0000J00ENG.html", "When harness connector of accelerator pedal position sensor is disconnected, perform “ACCELERATOR PEDAL RELEASED POSITION LEARNING”. Refer to Description.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801Z0000K00ENG.html", "Inspection", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801Z0000K00ENG.html", "INSPECTION AFTER INSTALLATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801Z0000K00ENG.html", "Check accelerator pedal moves smoothly within the whole operation range when it is fully depressed and released.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801Z0000K00ENG.html", "Check accelerator pedal securely returns to the fully released position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5020801Z0000K00ENG.html", "For the electrical inspection of accelerator pedal position sensor. Refer to .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "GENERAL DESCRIPTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "The 1.5L 4B40 engine features 4-cylinder, 16-valve, and double overhead camshafts (DOHC).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "The engine has the following features.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Aluminum cylinder block", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Resin water jacket spacer", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "MIVEC (Mitsubishi Innovative Valve timing Electronic Control system)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Selective valve tappet of direct acting valve system for valve clearance adjustment", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Exhaust manifold integrated with the cylinder head", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Timing chain", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Vacuum pump", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "Pendulum-type drive belt auto-tensioner", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390010000Q00ENG.html", "48V MILD HYBRID", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "MAIN SPECIFICATIONS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Specification", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Engine model", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "4B40", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Total displacement mL", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "1,499", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Bore × stroke mm", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "75.0 × 84.8", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Compression ratio", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "10.5", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Combustion chamber", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Pentroof type", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Valve timing", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Inlet opening", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "BTDC 51° - ATDC 9°", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Inlet closing", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "ABDC 1° - ABDC 61°", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Exhaust opening", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "BBDC 31° - BBDC 11°", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Exhaust closing", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "ATDC 5° - ATDC 25°", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Maximum output kW / r/min", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "130 / 5,000", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Maximum torque N·m / r/min", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "280 / 3,000 - 4,000", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Fuel injection system", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Electronically controlled multiport fuel injection and direct injection", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Ignition system", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390020000R00ENG.html", "Electronically controlled 4-coil", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390030000I00ENG.html", "ENGINE PERFORMANCE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CYLINDER HEAD RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CYLINDER HEAD COVER", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "A plastic cylinder head cover has been adopted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "PCV VALVE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CAMSHAFT BEARING CAP", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "The intake camshafts is supported by 5 bearings.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "The exhaust camshafts is supported by 6 bearings.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CYLINDER HEAD", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "The cylinder head is made of aluminum alloy, which is lightweight and has an excellent cooling efficiency. The inlet and exhaust ports are arranged in a cross-flow construction. Each cylinder has a pair of inlet ports on one side and a pair of exhaust ports on the other side.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CYLINDER HEAD GASKET", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "A multiple layers, metal type cylinder head gasket that excels in heat resistance and sealing performance has been adopted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "VALVE GUIDE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "Different valve guides are used on the intake and exhaust sides.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "VALVE SEAT", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "Sintered alloy valve seats have been adopted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390050000W00ENG.html", "CAMSHAFT POSITION SENSOR", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "CYLINDER BLOCK RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "CYLINDER BLOCK", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The cylinder block is made of aluminum alloy has been adopted for weight reduction.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The water jacket is the full siamese type.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Specification", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Overall height mm", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "279.59", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Bore mm", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "75.0", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Bore pitch mm", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "83.0", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "Stroke mm", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "84.8", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "WATER JACKET SPACER", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "A water jacket spacer made of resin has been adopted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The coolant flow in each cylinder is optimized by inserting the water jacket spacer directly into the water jacket of the cylinder block.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The water jacket spacer promotes the coolant flow to the exhaust side where the temperature is high, and enables to equalize the wall surface temperature of the upper area and the lower area of the cylindrical hole of the cylinder block.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "CRANKSHAFT BEARING CAP", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The crankshaft journal is supported by 5 bearings. The crankshaft thrust load is supported by No. 4 bearing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "OIL JET", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390060000O00ENG.html", "The oil jet cooling the piston is placed on the cylinder block lower plane which is the main bearing among cylinders.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "PISTON RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "PISTON", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "The pistons are made of special aluminum alloy. Their weight has been reduced by lowering their overall height and increasing the depression at each end of the piston pin. The piston pin hole center is offset 0.5 mm towards the thrust side of the piston center. The skirt portion along the perimeter of the piston is finished with streaks that excel in oil retention and seizure resistance.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "PISTON PIN", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "The full floating type of piston pin is used to improve the reliability by reducing the friction.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "CONNECTING ROD", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "The connecting rod is made of highly rigid, forged carbon steel. The rod portion has an H-shaped cross section. The connecting rod big end bearing is lubricated through an oil passage running from the main journal to the crankshaft pin.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "PISTON RING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "Each piston is provided with No. 1 and No. 2 compression rings and an oil ring.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "CONNECTING ROD BEARING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390070000O00ENG.html", "Adopted resin coating for upper connecting rod. The connecting rod bearing is equipped with back metal. While the bearing itself is made of aluminum alloy, the back metal is normally made of steel sheet. The connecting rod bearing is narrower than the bearing cap, this is to minimize wear.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "CRANKSHAFT RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "CRANK SHAFT", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "A forged crankshaft is used for the crankshaft. The crankshaft consists of five main bearings and eight balance weights. The crankshaft pins are arranged at 180° intervals. The oil hole supplies lubrication oil from the journal to the crank pin.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "CRANKSHAFT BEARING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "The upper crankshaft bearing (with oil groove) is located on the cylinder block side while the lower bearing (without oil groove) is held by the bearing cap. The crankshaft bearing is equipped with back metal. While the bearing itself is made of aluminum alloy, the back metal is made of steel sheet. A resin coat is added on the sliding surface to reduce friction &lt;No.1 bearing>. A molybdenum disulfide layer (shot treatment) is added on the sliding surface to reduce friction &lt;No.2 to 5 bearing>.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "THRUST BEARING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "A thrust bearing is installed on both sides of the No. 4 crankshaft bearing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "TORSIONAL VIBRATION DAMPER", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "The torsional vibration damper is made of cast-iron and rubber. The torsional vibration damper is equipped with a torsional damper to minimize the torsional vibration of the crankshaft as well as substantially reduce noise and vibration at the high speed range.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "CRANKSHAFT ISOLATION PULLEY", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "The crankshaft isolation pulley is made of iron and spring steel. The pulley has grooves to engage with a V-ribbed belt (seven ribs), which drives a belt drive starter generator and a water pump and an A/C compressor. The isolation pulley absorbs rotational fluctuations by means of a spring.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "CRANKSHAFT SENSING RING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "The crankshaft is also fitted with a crankshaft sensing ring.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "DRIVE PLATE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "A cast iron ring gear is a shrink fit in the steel plate of the drive plate. The drive plate is installed by tightening six bolts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390080000O00ENG.html", "ADAPTER PLATE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "TIMING CHAIN RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "OIL SEAL", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "A front crankshaft oil seal is press-fit into the case.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "TIMING CHAIN CASE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "The oil pump and the relief valve are integrated as well as water chamber of the water pump.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "TIMING CHAIN", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "Two camshafts are driven by the timing chain via the respective sprockets. The timing chain, consisting of 122 links, is an endless chain, connecting the crankshaft sprocket with the camshaft and V.V.T. sprockets. The timing chain is equipped with three mark link plates to correctly time the two sprockets with each other. The timing chain is tensioned by the timing chain tensioner, which has a built-in plunger with plunger springs.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "TIMING CHAIN TENSIONER", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "The plunger in the timing chain tensioner directly pushes the tension lever, and the pressure automatically adjusts the timing chain tension. A cam is provided to lock the plunger in place after the engine stops. This helps to prevent the timing chain from wobbling just after the engine starts. With the timing chain tensioner installed, do not crank the engine in the reverse direction. This will force the plunger to overcome the cam, or even cause other problems.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "TENSION LEVER ASSEMBLY", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "CHAIN GUIDE ASSEMBLY", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390090000O00ENG.html", "V.V.T. SPROCKET", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "VALVE RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "The valve mechanism is based on a 4-valve DOHC (Double Over Head Camshaft) design having the camshaft on the upper valve. Each cylinder has two inlet valves and two exhaust valves, arranged in a V-shape pattern.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "Camshaft rotation is transmitted via valve tappets to the respective valves which open and close accordingly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "CAMSHAFT", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "VALVE TAPPET", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "Valve tappets are available in 31 thicknesses, at 0.020 mm intervals between 2.700 mm  and 3.300 mm, to ensure the correct valve clearance.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "VALVE", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "The valves have heat-resistance. The entire valve surface is treated with nitriding.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "VALVE STEM SEAL", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "The valve stem seal portion excels in sealing performance and is equipped with a spring to prevent oil from descending.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "VALVE SPRING", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390100000O00ENG.html", "The valve spring has a dual pitch spring to prevent surging in the high speed range.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "MIVEC (MITSUBISHI INNOVATIVE VALVE TIMING ELECTRONIC CONTROL SYSTEM) RELATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "MIVEC (Mitsubishi Innovative Valve timing Electronic Control system) consists of the components illustrated above.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "The valve timing is optimally controlled (continuously variable) under the changing driving conditions to improve performance in the entire speed range.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "V.V.T. SPROCKET (VARIABLE VALVE TIMING SPROCKET)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "Oil from the engine oil control valve is sent to the V.V.T. sprocket, moving the vane rotor and thus regulating the valve timing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "CAMSHAFT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "The lightweight camshaft is achieved by the hollow design.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "Oil channels run through the camshaft, through which oil is sent from the engine oil control valve to the V.V.T. sprocket.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "A cam position sensing ring is press-fitted onto the rear portion of the camshaft.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "ENGINE OIL CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "The engine oil control valve is essentially a solenoid valve, regulated by the ECM signals to feed oil to the V.V.T. sprocket assembly to move the vane rotor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502390110000W00ENG.html", "By adopting a filter-equipped engine oil control valve, a filter is added to each port to improve reliability.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "VACUUM PUMP", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "The vacuum pump is installed to the rear end of the inlet camshaft to secure the brake booster vacuum.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "Specification", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "Type", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "Single vane pump", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "Discharge amount L/rev", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391520000H00ENG.html", "0.13", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391560000G00ENG.html", "DRIVE BELT AUTO-TENSIONER", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391560000G00ENG.html", "Due to the adoption of the belt drive starter generator, a pendulum-type auto-tensioner, which can be used for engine start and power generation, has been adopted. The auto-tensioner is installed to the front side of the belt drive starter generator.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502391010001900ENG.html", "SERVICE SPECIFICATIONS", "title");
