si[i++] = gsitm("N502500050000A00ENG.html", "Ignition switch-IG", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500080000400ENG.html", "AIR FLOW SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500080000400ENG.html", "The air flow sensor is installed to the air cleaner assembly and is placed in the stream of intake air. It measures the intake flow rate by measuring a part of the entire intake flow. The air flow sensor controls the temperature of the heater in sensing element to a certain amount. The temperature distribution around the heater changes according to the increase in intake air volume. The change is detected by a thermistor and the air volume data is frequency modulated by the signal processing circuit in the air flow sensor and sent to the ECM. The ECM uses this output signal and engine speed to calculate and decide basic fuel injection time. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "NO. 1 INTAKE AIR TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "The No. 1 intake air temperature sensor is built-into air flow sensor. The sensor detects intake air temperature. The temperature sensing unit uses a thermistor which is sensitive to the change in temperature. The detected intake air temperature is converted to a voltage according to the intake air temperature by the signal processing circuit in the air flow sensor and the voltage is output to the ECM. The ECM uses this output signal and engine speed to calculate and decide basic fuel injection time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "&lt;Reference data>", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "Intake air temperature", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "Sensor output voltage", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "25°C", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500090000400ENG.html", "Approx. 2 V", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000A0000300ENG.html", "BOOST PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000A0000300ENG.html", "The boost pressure sensor is installed in the intercooler assembly. The boost pressure sensor uses a piezo resistive semiconductor to output the voltage according to supercharging pressure to the ECM. The ECM uses this output voltage and manifold absolute pressure sensor output to decide throttle valve opening angle and waste gate valve opening angle. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000B0000400ENG.html", "NO. 2 INTAKE AIR TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000B0000400ENG.html", "The No. 2 intake air temperature sensor is built in to the boost pressure sensor. The No. 2 intake air temperature sensor detects intake air temperature through thermistor\'s resistance change and outputs the voltage according to intake air temperature to the ECM. The ECM uses this output voltage to compensate fuel injection control. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000C0000300ENG.html", "MANIFOLD ABSOLUTE PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000C0000300ENG.html", "The manifold absolute pressure sensor is installed in the inlet manifold. The manifold absolute pressure sensor uses a piezo resistive semiconductor to output the voltage according to manifold absolute pressure to the ECM. The ECM uses this output voltage to compensate fuel injection volume according to manifold absolute pressure. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000D0000400ENG.html", "NO. 3 INTAKE AIR TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000D0000400ENG.html", "The No. 3 intake air temperature sensor is built in to the manifold absolute pressure sensor. The No. 3 intake air temperature sensor detects intake air temperature through thermistor\'s resistance change and outputs the voltage according to intake air temperature to the ECM. The ECM uses this output voltage to compensate fuel injection control and ignition timing control. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000E0000300ENG.html", "ENGINE COOLANT TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000E0000300ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature sensor is installed to the water outlet fitting located at the rear end of the cylinder head. The engine coolant temperature sensor uses thermistor\'s resistance change to detect coolant temperature and output the voltage according to coolant temperature to the ECM. The ECM uses this output voltage to appropriately control fuel injection volume, idle speed and ignition timing when the engine is cold. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000V0000400ENG.html", "INTERCOOLER COOLANT TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000V0000400ENG.html", "The intercooler coolant temperature sensor is installed to the water temperature sensor housing which is provided on the upper side of the inlet manifold. The intercooler coolant temperature sensor uses thermistor\'s resistance change to detect the temperature of the coolant which enters the intercooler and outputs the voltage according to coolant temperature to the ECM. Based on the output voltage, the ECM performs drive control of the electric water pump. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "THROTTLE POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "The throttle position sensor is installed in the throttle body. The throttle position sensor outputs voltage to the ECM based on the throttle shaft rotation angle. The ECM uses this signal to detect the throttle valve opening angle to perform Throttle valve control servo feedback control. This throttle position sensor uses Hall IC and is a non-contact type.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "STRUCTURE AND SYSTEM", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "The throttle position sensor is composed of a permanent magnet fixed on the throttle shaft, Hall IC that outputs voltage according to magnetic flux density and a stator that efficiently introduces magnetic flux from the permanent magnet to Hall IC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "Magnetic flux density at Hall IC is proportional to the output voltage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "Throttle position sensor has 2 output systems - throttle position sensor (main) and throttle position sensor (sub), and the output voltage is output to the ECM. When throttle valve turns, output voltage of throttle position sensor (main) and throttle position sensor (sub) changes. This allows ECM to detect actual throttle opening angle. The ECM uses this output voltage for Throttle valve control servo feedback control. The relationship between throttle opening angle and output voltage of the throttle position sensor (main) and throttle position sensor (sub) is as shown in the figure below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "When abnormality is detected", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "The ECM compares output voltage of the throttle position sensor (main) and throttle position sensor (sub) to check for abnormality in the throttle position sensor. If the ECM detects the abnormality, the emergency should be prevented by performing the fail-safe control.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "When 1-system malfunctions", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "The ECM should perform the throttle valve position control by only using the signal having no malfunctions. Limit the accelerator pedal to half. Performing the fuel cut can suppress increase the engine rotation speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "When 2-system malfunctions", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000F0000300ENG.html", "The ECM should cut the energization of the throttle valve control servo. At that time, the spring built in the throttle valve can slightly open the throttle valve. This allows the ECM to control the engine output.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "ACCELERATOR PEDAL POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "The accelerator pedal position sensor is installed on the upper end of the accelerator pedal assembly. The sensor detects the accelerator position and sends a signal to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "Accelerator pedal position sensor has two sensors (main, sub). These sensors are a kind of potentiometers which transform the accelerator pedal position into output voltage, and emit the voltage signal to the ECM. In addition, these sensors detect the opening and closing speed of the accelerator pedal and feed the voltage signals to the ECM. The ECM judges the current opening angle of the accelerator pedal from these signals and controls the throttle control motor based on these signals.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "Idle position of the accelerator pedal is determined by the ECM receiving the signal from the accelerator pedal position sensor. The ECM uses this signal for the engine operation such as fuel cut.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "When abnormality is detected", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "The ECM compares output voltage of the accelerator pedal position sensor (main) and accelerator pedal position sensor (sub) to check for abnormality in sensor. If the ECM detects the abnormality, the emergency should be prevented by performing the fail-safe control.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "When 1-system malfunctions", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "The ECM should detect the amount of accelerator pedal depressed by only using the signal having no malfunctions. Limit the accelerator pedal to half. Performing the fuel cut suppress increase the engine rotation speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "When 2-system malfunctions", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000G0000300ENG.html", "The ECM should cut the energization of the throttle valve control servo. At that time, the spring built in the throttle valve can slightly open the throttle valve. This allows the ECM to control the engine output.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000H0000400ENG.html", "LINEAR A/F SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000H0000400ENG.html", "The linear A/F sensor is installed to the upstream side of the catalytic converter which is located under the turbocharger. This sensor detects the oxygen concentration in the exhaust gas by a solid electrolyte (zirconia). It can detect the air-fuel ratio in the wide range from the lean air-fuel ratio to the rich air-fuel ratio. The ECM measures the air-fuel ratio by measuring electrical current when the voltage is applied to the linear A/F sensor. Therefore, the ECM can accurately perform the feedback control to the air-fuel ratio so that the three-way catalytic conversion efficiency can reach the best theoretical air-fuel ratio.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000H0000400ENG.html", "To activate elements, this sensor integrates the heater. The ECM controls the electrical current going through the heater.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000J0000400ENG.html", "OXYGEN SENSOR (REAR)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000J0000400ENG.html", "The oxygen sensor (rear) is installed to the upstream side of the catalytic converter which is located under the floor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000J0000400ENG.html", "The heated oxygen sensor has a built-in heater to help early activation of the sensor. This allows feedback control of air-fuel ratio soon after engine start.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000J0000400ENG.html", "This sensor uses the oxygen concentration cell principle of solid electrolyte (zirconia) and displays the property of sudden change in output voltage near theoretical air-fuel ratio. This property is used to detect oxygen density in exhaust gas. Feedback to the ECM allows it to judge whether air-fuel ratio is rich or lean compared to theoretical air-fuel ratio.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000J0000400ENG.html", "This allows the ECM precise feedback control to get theoretical air-fuel ratio with best cleaning efficiency of 3-way catalytic converter.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000K0000400ENG.html", "CRANK ANGLE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000K0000400ENG.html", "The crank angle sensor is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder block. The crank angle sensor monitors rotation of crankshaft sensing ring (60 teeth including 2 missing teeth) installed on the crankshaft and converts to voltage (pulse signal) that is output to the ECM. The ECM uses crank angle sensor\'s output pulse to detect crank angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000K0000400ENG.html", "The crank angle sensor uses a magnetic resistance element. When the vane of the crankshaft sensing ring passes the front surface of the magnetic resistance element, the flux from the magnet passes the magnetic resistance element. Thus, resistance of the magnetic resistance element increases. When the vane of the crankshaft sensing ring does not pass the front surface of the magnetic resistance element, the flux from the magnet does not pass the magnetic resistance element and the resistance decreases. The crank angle sensor converts this change in resistance of the magnetic resistance element to a 5 V pulse signal and outputs it to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000L0000400ENG.html", "INTAKE CAMSHAFT POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000L0000400ENG.html", "The intake camshaft position sensor is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder head. The intake camshaft position sensor monitors rotation of the camshaft position sensing ring (3 teeth) and converts to voltage (pulse signal) that is output to the ECM. Upon receiving this output voltage, the ECM effects feedback control to optimize the phase of the inlet camshaft. The ECM uses a combination of the intake camshaft position sensor output pulse signal and crank angle sensor output pulse signal to identify cylinders in the compression process.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000L0000400ENG.html", "The camshaft position sensor uses a magnetic resistance element. When the vane of the camshaft position sensing ring passes the front surface of the magnetic resistance element, the flux from the magnet passes the magnetic resistance element. Thus, the resistance of the magnetic resistance element increases. When the vane of the camshaft position sensing ring does not pass the front surface of the magnetic resistance element, the flux from the magnet does not pass to magnetic resistance element and resistance decreases. The camshaft position sensor converts this change in resistance of the magnetic resistance element to a 5 V pulse signal and outputs the signal to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000M0000300ENG.html", "EXHAUST CAMSHAFT POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000M0000300ENG.html", "The exhaust camshaft position sensor is installed on the exhaust side of the cylinder head. The exhaust camshaft position sensor monitors rotation of the exhaust camshaft position sensing ring (3 teeth) and converts to voltage (pulse signal) that is output to ECM. Upon receiving this output voltage, the ECM effects feedback control to optimize the phase of the exhaust camshaft.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000N0000400ENG.html", "DETONATION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000N0000400ENG.html", "The detonation sensor is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder block. The detonation sensor uses the piezoelectric element to convert the vibration of the cylinder block generated when engine is in operation to minute voltage that is output to the ECM. The ECM uses the minute output voltage from the detonation sensor filtered through the cylinder block\'s natural frequency to detect knocking, and compensates the ignition timing lag according to the strength of the knocking.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000O0000400ENG.html", "WASTE GATE POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000O0000400ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Intake and Exhaust, Description, Exhaust System, Turbocharger", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000P0000400ENG.html", "FUEL PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000P0000400ENG.html", "The fuel pressure sensor is installed in the delivery pipe  (high pressure). It uses a semiconductor to output a voltage according to the fuel pressure in the delivery pipe  (high pressure) to the ECM. The ECM takes feedback control on the pressure control valve in accordance with this voltage output. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000P0000400ENG.html", "Do not remove the fuel pressure sensor from the delivery pipe  (high pressure).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Q0000300ENG.html", "BAROMETRIC PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Q0000300ENG.html", "The barometric pressure sensor is built into the ECM. The barometric pressure sensor is a semiconductor diffused pressure element which outputs voltage to the ECM according to atmospheric pressure. The ECM uses this output voltage to sense the altitude of the vehicle and compensates fuel injection volume to achieve the appropriate air-fuel ratio for that altitude.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000X0000500ENG.html", "ENGINE OIL PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000X0000500ENG.html", "The engine oil pressure sensor is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder block.It uses a semiconductor to output a voltage according to the engine oil pressure to the ECM.ECM uses this voltage output for controlling oil relief control valve. Sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Y0000301ENG.html", "ENGINE OIL PRESSURE SWITCH", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Y0000301ENG.html", "The engine oil pressure switch is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder block. The engine oil pressure switch detects whether the oil pressure is high or low using the contact switch. When the oil pressure becomes higher than the specified value after the engine starts, the contact point of the engine oil pressure switch opens.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Y0000301ENG.html", "This allows the ECM to detect the oil pressure is higher than the specified value. The ECM outputs the OFF signal to the combination meter through the CAN and then turns off the oil pressure warning light.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000W0000300ENG.html", "A/C PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000W0000300ENG.html", "The A/C pressure sensor is installed to the liquid pipe assembly which is located on the outlet side of the A/C condenser. The A/C pressure sensor detects the refrigerant pressure (A/C load) and outputs the voltage corresponding to the refrigerant pressure to the ECM. The sensor uses an electrostatic volume pressure transducer to convert refrigerant pressure to voltage. The ECM uses this output voltage to calculate correction torque of the A/C compressor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Z0000300ENG.html", "BRAKE MONITORING SWITCH", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Z0000300ENG.html", "The brake monitoring switch is unified with stoplight switch and is installed on the brake pedal. The brake monitoring switch is a contact-type switch and detects whether the brake pedal is depressed. When the brake pedal is depressed, the contact point of the brake monitoring switch should open.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000Z0000300ENG.html", "This allows the ECM to detect the brake pedal depressed, and the ECM performs operations such as cancellation of the cruise control.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500120000800ENG.html", "FUEL TANK PRESSURE SENSOR &lt;VEHICLES FOR TAIWAN>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500120000800ENG.html", "The fuel tank pressure sensor is installed to the canister and detects the pressure in the purge line.The fuel tank pressure sensor outputs voltage corresponding to the pressure to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500120000800ENG.html", "When monitoring the evaporative leak, the ECM detects malfunctions of the evaporative emission control system by monitoring the amount of output voltage changes from this sensor. The sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500120000800ENG.html", "Diagnosis item name \"Canister Pressure Sensor\" and \"Evaporative Emission Control System Pressure Sensor\" of diagnosis code, which are shown on the M.U.T.-III SE display and described in the Workshop Manual, indicate fuel tank pressure sensor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500130000300ENG.html", "FUEL TANK TEMPERATURE SENSOR &lt;VEHICLES FOR TAIWAN>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500130000300ENG.html", "Fuel tank temperature sensor is installed to the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly. The fuel tank temperature sensor uses thermistor\'s resistance change to detect the fuel temperature in the fuel tank and outputs the voltage according to the fuel temperature to the ECM. The ECM monitors the evaporative leak in accordance with the fuel tank temperature.Sensor properties are as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500140000300ENG.html", "CRUISE CONTROL SWITCH", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500140000300ENG.html", "&lt;Vehicles without ACC>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500140000300ENG.html", "&lt;Vehicles with ACC>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500140000300ENG.html", "The cruise control switch is installed to the right-side spoke part of the steering wheel.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500140000300ENG.html", "Cruise control switch has variant values of electrical resistance for each button. ECM reads voltage variation of switch, and determines which button is operated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000R0000300ENG.html", "MULTI FLOW CONTROL VALVE POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000R0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine Cooling, Description .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000S0000300ENG.html", "EGR POSITION SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000S0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000U0000300ENG.html", "EGR DIFFERENTIAL PRESSURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000U0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000T0000400ENG.html", "EGR GAS TEMPERATURE SENSOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025000T0000400ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500160000A00ENG.html", "FUEL INJECTOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500160000A00ENG.html", "The fuel injector is an injection nozzle with a solenoid valve that injects fuel into the intake pipe of the cylinder head based on the injection signal sent from the ECM. One fuel injector is installed in the top of the intake port in the cylinder head of each cylinder and fixed to the delivery pipe . When electricity flows through the solenoid coil, the needle gets sucked in. The needle gets pulled till the fully open position so that the injection hole is fully open and the fuel gets injected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500160000A00ENG.html", "The voltage from the battery is applied from the ECM relay (inside the IPDM E/R) to the fuel injector relay, the fuel injector and up to the ECM. ECM turns ON its power transistor and prepares the fuel injector\'s ground circuit. Thus, current flows through the fuel injector while power transistor is ON and the fuel injector injects fuel.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500170000A00ENG.html", "FUEL INJECTOR (HIGH PRESSURE)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500170000A00ENG.html", "The fuel injector (high pressure) is an injection nozzle with a solenoid valve that injects fuel into the cylinder based on the injection signal sent from the ECM. One fuel injector (high pressure) is installed in the bottom of the intake port in the cylinder head of each cylinder and fixed to the delivery pipe  (high pressure). When electricity flows through the solenoid coil, the needle gets sucked in. The needle is pulled up to the fully open position, and the injection port is fully opened and fuel is injected. The multi-hole injection port is adopted to the fuel injector (high pressure). This atomizes the fuel spray, improving fuel economy and reducing CO2.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500170000A00ENG.html", "Voltage boosted by the ECM is applied to the driving voltage of the fuel injector (high pressure). The ECM turns ON the power transistor in the ECM to create the ground circuit of the injector. As a result, current flows through the fuel injector (high pressure) while the power transistor is ON, and the fuel injector (high pressure) injects fuel.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500180000400ENG.html", "THROTTLE VALVE CONTROL SERVO", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500180000400ENG.html", "A throttle valve control servo is installed in throttle body. The throttle valve control servo performs the Open/Close of the throttle valve through the reduction gear. ECM changes current direction according to the Open/Close direction and also changes current to the motor coil in order to the control throttle valve control servo.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500180000400ENG.html", "Throttle valve control servo is composed of a good response, low energy, and small DC motor with brush and can generate rotation force corresponding to the current applied on the coil. When there is no current passing through the throttle valve control servo, the throttle valve remains at a prescribed opening angle. So, even if current stops because of a fault in the system a minimum level of running remains possible.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500190000400ENG.html", "INLET OIL FEEDER CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500190000400ENG.html", "The inlet oil feeder control valve is installed on the inlet side of the cylinder head. Receiving the duty signal from the ECM, the inlet oil feeder control valve moves the spool valve position and divides the oil pressure from the cylinder block into the advanced chamber and the retarded chamber of the V.V.T. sprocket as well as continually changes the inlet camshaft phase. The spring makes spool valve stop at the position where the inlet camshaft is at the most retarded angle when the engine is stopped. The ECM operates the spool valve position by increasing and decreasing ON duty ratio of the inlet oil feeder control valve and allows the inlet camshaft to be at the target phase angle. When the duty ratio increases, the V.V.T. sprocket makes phase of inlet camshaft advanced angle side. When the duty ratio decreases, the V.V.T. sprocket makes phase of inlet camshaft retarded angle side. When the medium duty ratio, at which the spool valve is at the medium position, is achieved, all the oil passages are closed. This allows the phase angle to be kept constant. The ECM changes and controls the duty ratio in accordance with the engine operation to get the optimum phase angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001A0000400ENG.html", "EXHAUST OIL FEEDER CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001A0000400ENG.html", "The exhaust oil feeder control valve is installed on the exhaust side of the cylinder head. Receiving the duty signal from the ECM, the exhaust oil feeder control valve moves the spool valve position and divides the oil pressure from the cylinder block into the advanced chamber and the retarded chamber of the V.V.T. sprocket as well as continually changes the exhaust camshaft phase. The spring makes spool valve stop at the position where the exhaust camshaft is at the most advanced angle when the engine is stopped. The ECM operates the spool valve position by increasing and decreasing ON duty ratio of the exhaust oil feeder control valve and allows the exhaust camshaft to be at the target phase angle. When the duty ratio increases, the V.V.T. sprocket makes phase of exhaust camshaft retarded angle side. When the duty ratio decreases, the V.V.T. sprocket makes phase of exhaust camshaft advanced angle side. When the medium duty ratio, at which the spool valve is at the medium position, is achieved, all the oil passages are closed. This allows the phase angle to be kept constant. The ECM changes and controls the duty ratio in accordance with the engine operation to get the optimum phase angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001B0000300ENG.html", "FUEL PUMP (HIGH PRESSURE)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001B0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Fuel Supply, Description, Fuel Pump (High Pressure) .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001C0000400ENG.html", "WASTE GATE ACTUATOR CONTROL SERVO", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001C0000400ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Intake and Exhaust, Description, Exhaust System, Turbocharger .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001D0000300ENG.html", "IGNITION COIL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001D0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine Electrical, Description, Ignition System, Ignition Coil .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001E0000300ENG.html", "EXHAUST GAS RECIRCULATION (EGR) VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001E0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Exhaust Gas Recirculation System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001F0000300ENG.html", "MULTI FLOW CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001F0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine Cooling, Description, Multi Flow Control Valve .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001G0000300ENG.html", "OIL RELIEF CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001G0000300ENG.html", "The oil relief control valve is incorporated into the timing chain case and it varies the oil pump capacity to control the discharge amount.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001G0000300ENG.html", "The ECM controls the drive duty rate of the oil relief control valve to optimize the hydraulic pressure according to the driving conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001J0000300ENG.html", "ELECTRIC WATER PUMP", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001J0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine - Intake and Exhaust - Description - Air Intake System - Intercooler - .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001K0000800ENG.html", "48V BATTERY FAN & MOTOR", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001K0000800ENG.html", "48V battery fan & motor is installed on the DC-DC converter and it is provided to cool the 48V battery and the DC-DC converter.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001K0000800ENG.html", "The driving rotation speed of the 48V battery fan & motor is controlled according to the PWM signal from the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001K0000800ENG.html", "In addition, the 48V battery fan & motor sends the motor rotation speed signal to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012V0000300ENG.html", "ACTIVE GRILL SHUTTER", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012V0000300ENG.html", "Refer to Body Exterior, Doors, Roof & Vehicle Security Exterior, System Description, Component Parts, Active Grill Shutter System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001H0000400ENG.html", "PURGE CONTROL SOLENOID VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001H0000400ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Evaporative Emission Control System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001I0000400ENG.html", "VENTILATION SOLENOID VALVE &lt;VEHICLES FOR TAIWAN>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001I0000400ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Description, Evaporative Emission Control System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "FUEL INJECTION CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel injection volume is regulated to obtain the optimum air-fuel ratio in accordance with the constant minute changes in engine driving conditions. Fuel injection volume is controlled by fuel injector drive time (injection time). There is a prescribed basic drive time that varies according to the engine speed and intake air volume. ECM adds prescribed compensations to this basic drive time according to conditions such as the intake air temperature and engine coolant temperature to decide injection time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "1. FUEL INJECTOR ACTUATION (FUEL INJECTION) TIMING", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel injector drive time in case of direct injection and multipoint fuel injection (DI and MPI) is controlled as follows according to driving conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel Injection During Cranking and Normal Operation (MFI)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel Injection During Normal Operation [DFI(Intake) and MFI]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel Injection During Normal Operation [DFI(Intake), DFI(Compression) and MFI]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel injection to each cylinder is done by driving the fuel injector and the fuel injector (high pressure) at optimum timing based on the crank angle sensor signal. ECM compares the crank angle sensor output pulse signal and inlet camshaft position sensor output pulse signal to identify the cylinder. Using this as a base, it performs sequential injection in the sequence of cylinders 1, 3, 4, 2. In addition, the fuel injection mode changes with driving conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Additional Fuel Injection During Acceleration", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "In addition to the synchronizing fuel injection with the crank angle sensor signal during acceleration, the volume of fuel is injected according to the extent of the acceleration.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "2. Fuel injection volume (fuel injector drive time) control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Under normal operating conditions, the figure shows the flow chart of calculating the injection amount during the fuel injector driving time. Basic drive time is decided based on the air flow sensor signal (intake air volume signal) and crank angle sensor signal (engine rotation signal). This basic drive time is compensated according to signals from various sensors and optimum fuel injector drive time (fuel injection volume) is calculated according to driving conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel Injection Volume Control Block Diagram (Normal Operation)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "[Fuel injector basic drive time]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Fuel injection is performed once per cycle for each cylinder. Basic drive time refers to fuel injection volume (fuel injector drive time) to achieve theoretical air-fuel ratio for the intake air volume of 1 cycle of 1 cylinder. Fuel injection volume changes according to the pressure difference (injected fuel pressure) between manifold pressure and fuel pressure (constant). So, injected fuel pressure compensation is made to fuel injector drive time for theoretical air-fuel ratio to arrive at basic drive time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Intake air volume of each cycle of 1 cylinder is calculated by ECM based on the air flow sensor signal and crank angle sensor signal. Also, during engine start, the map value prescribed by the coolant temperature sensor signal is used as basic drive time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "[Fuel injector drive time compensation]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "After calculating the fuel injector basic drive time, the ECM makes the following compensations to control the optimum fuel injection volume according to driving conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "List of main compensations for fuel injection control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensations", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Content", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Linear A/F sensor feedback compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "The linear A/F sensor signal is used for making the compensation to get air-fuel ratio with best cleaning efficiency of the 3-way catalytic converter. This compensation might not be made sometimes in order to improve drivability, depending on driving conditions. (Air-fuel ratio compensation is made.) The ECM compensates the output signal of the linear A/F sensor using the output signal of the oxygen sensor (rear). This allows the deviation of the output signal, caused by the deterioration of the linear A/F sensor, to be solved, then the highly accurate exhaust gas control is performed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Air-fuel ratio compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Under driving conditions where linear A/F sensor feedback compensation is not performed, compensation is made based on pre-set map values that vary according to engine speed and intake air volume.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Engine coolant temperature compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to the engine coolant temperature. The lower the engine coolant temperature, the greater the fuel injection volume.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Acceleration/ Deceleration compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to change in intake air volume. During acceleration, fuel injection volume is increased. Also, during deceleration, fuel injection volume is decreased.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Intake air temperature compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to the intake air temperature. The lower the intake air temperature, the greater the fuel injection volume.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Barometric pressure compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to the barometric pressure. The lower the barometric pressure, the smaller the fuel injection volume.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Battery voltage compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made depending on battery voltage. The lower the battery voltage, the greater the fuel injector drive signal time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Intake air temperature and pressure in inlet manifold compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to the intake air temperature and pressure in the inlet manifold.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Learning value for fuel compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "Compensation amount is learned to compensate feedback of oxygen sensor. This allows system to compensate in accordance with engine characteristics.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "[Fuel limit control during deceleration]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "ECM limits fuel when decelerating downhill to prevent excessive rise of catalytic converter temperature and to improve fuel efficiency.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "[Fuel-cut control when over-run]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001L0000300ENG.html", "When engine speed exceeds a prescribed limit (6,300 r/min), ECM cuts fuel supply to prevent overrunning and thus protect the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "IGNITION TIMING AND CONTROL FOR CURRENT CARRYING TIME", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Ignition timing is pre-set according to engine driving conditions. Compensations are made according to pre-set values depending on conditions such as engine coolant temperature, battery voltage etc. to decide optimum ignition timing. Primary current connect/disconnect signal is sent to the power transistor to control ignition timing. Ignition is done in sequence of cylinders 1, 3, 4, 2.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "1. Ignition power control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Based on the crank angle sensor signal and inlet camshaft position sensor signal, ECM decides the ignition cylinder, calculates the ignition timing and sends the ignition coil primary current connect/disconnect signal to the power transistor of each cylinder in the ignition sequence.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "2. Spark-advance control and current carrying time control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "[During start]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "ECM initiates ignition at fixed ignition timing (4° BTDC) synchronised with the crank angle sensor signal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "[During normal operation]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "After determining the basic spark-advance based on the intake air volume and engine speed, ECM makes compensations based on input from various sensors to control the optimum spark-advance and current carrying time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "List of main compensations for spark-advance control and current carrying time control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensations", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Content", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Intake air temperature compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to intake air temperature. The higher the intake air temperature the greater the delay in ignition timing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Engine coolant temperature compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to engine coolant temperature. The lower the engine coolant temperature the greater the advance in ignition timing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Knocking compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to generation of knocking. The greater the knocking the greater the delay in ignition timing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Stable idle compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to change in idle speed. In case engine speed becomes lower than target speed, ignition timing is advanced.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Delay compensation when changing shift", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "During change of shift, sparking is delayed compared to normal ignition timing to reduce engine output torque and absorb the shock of the shift change.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Battery voltage compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made depending on battery voltage. The lower the battery voltage the greater the current carrying time and when battery voltage is high current carrying time is shortened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "[Control for checking ignition timing]", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001M0000300ENG.html", "During basic ignition timing set mode for M.U.T.-III SE actuator test function, sparking is done with fixed ignition timing (5° BTDC) synchronised with crank angle sensor signal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "THROTTLE VALVE OPENING ANGLE CONTROL AND IDLE SPEED CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "ECM detects the amount of accelerator pedal depression (as per operator\'s intention) through the accelerator pedal position sensor. Based on pre-set basic target opening angles it adds various compensations and controls the throttle valve opening angle according to the target opening angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "While starting", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "ECM adds various compensations to the target opening angle that is set based on the engine coolant temperature, so that the air volume is optimum for starting.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "While idling", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "ECM controls the throttle valve to achieve the target opening angle that is set based on the engine coolant temperature. In this way best idle operation is achieved when engine is cold and when it is hot. Also, the following compensations ensure optimum control.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "While driving", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Compensations are made to the target opening angle set according to the accelerator pedal opening angle and engine speed to control the throttle valve opening angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "List of main compensations for throttle valve opening angle and idle speed control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Compensations", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Content", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Stable idle compensation (immediately after start)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "In order to stabilize idle speed immediately after start, target opening angle is kept big and then gradually reduced. Compensation values are set based on the engine coolant temperature.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Engine speed feedback compensation (while idling)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "In case there is a difference between the target idle speed and actual engine speed, ECM compensates the throttle valve opening angle based on that difference.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Barometric pressure compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "At high altitudes barometric pressure is less and the intake air density is low. So, the target opening angle is compensated based on barometric pressure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Engine coolant temperature compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Compensation is made according to the engine coolant temperature. The lower the engine coolant temperature the greater the throttle valve opening angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Electric load compensation", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Throttle valve opening angle is compensated according to electric load. The greater the electric load, the greater the throttle valve opening angle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Compensation when shift is in D range &lt;CVT>", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "When transmission is changed from P or N range to some other range, throttle valve opening angle is increased to prevent reduction in engine speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Compensation when A/C is functioning", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Throttle valve opening angle is compensated according to functioning of A/C compressor. While A/C compressor is being driven, the throttle valve opening angle is increased.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Initialise control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "After ignition switch turns OFF, ECM drives the throttle valve from fully closed position and records the fully closed and neutral position studied values of the throttle position sensor (main and sub) output signals. The recorded studied values are used as studied value compensation for compensating basic target opening angle when the engine is started next.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "Engine protection control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001N0000300ENG.html", "When the racing is continued during the vehicle stopped period (no-load period) for more than the specified time, the ECM closes the throttle valve and restricts the engine speed to protect the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "MIVEC (Mitsubishi Innovative Valve Timing Electronic Control System)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "MIVEC is a control system continuously varying the intake valve timing and exhaust valve timing. The opening and closing period of the valve does not change.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "MIVEC allows the optimum valve timing to be controlled in accordance with the engine operation and the idling stability to be improved, as well as the output and the torque to be better in all the operation ranges.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "The ECM assesses the engine operation through the signals from each sensor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Based on the assessed information, the ECM sends the duty signal to the inlet oil feeder control valve and the exhaust oil feeder control valve, and controls the spool valve position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Changing the spool valve position allows the oil pressure to be divided into the retarded chamber and the advanced chamber, as well as allows the phases of the inlet camshaft and the exhaust camshaft to be continuously changed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "The detected phase angle is calculated using the inlet camshaft position sensor signal and the exhaust camshaft position sensor signal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Operation Conceptual Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "The ECM controls the camshaft phase angle in order to attain optimal valve timing that suits the engine load and engine speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Initial phase", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Control direction", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Inlet side", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Most retarded angle", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Advance direction", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Exhaust side", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Most advanced angle", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001O0000300ENG.html", "Retard direction", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001P0000300ENG.html", "WASTE GATE CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001P0000300ENG.html", "Based on the waste gate valve basic target opening angle, which changes in accordance with the engine operation status, the ECM determines the optimum target opening angle by adding various corrections, and controls the waste gate actuator. This results in a supercharging pressure that suits the driving conditions of the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001P0000300ENG.html", "System configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001P0000300ENG.html", "Initialise control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001P0000300ENG.html", "After the ignition switch is turned ON, the ECM drives the waste gate valve to the fully closed position and stores the signal of the waste gate position sensor output at that time as the learned value for full closing. The stored learned value is used to correct the target opening angle as the learned value correction during engine operation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001Q0000800ENG.html", "ENGINE CONTROL MODULE (ECM) RELAY CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001Q0000800ENG.html", "When the ignition switch is turned ON, a 12V battery current flows to the ignition relay in the IPDM E/R, and the ignition relay is turned ON. When the ignition relay is turned ON and a voltage is applied to the ignition switch-IG terminal of the ECM, the ECM will turn ON the power transistor controlling the ECM relay. By doing so, auxiliary battery current is applied to the ECM relay coil in the IPDM E/R turning ON the ECM relay, and supplies power to each sensor and actuator.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001Q0000800ENG.html", "Throttle valve initialising control", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001R0000300ENG.html", "FUEL PUMP RELAY CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001R0000300ENG.html", "When the ignition switch is turned ON, a 12V battery current flows to the ignition relay in the IPDM E/R, and the ignition relay is turned ON. When a current is applied to the fuel pump relay in the IPDM E/R, the fuel pump relay is turned ON and the fuel pump is driven. When the ignition switch-ST signal is sent to the ECM from the BCM via CAN, the ECM will turn ON the power transistor controlling the fuel pump relay control. By doing so, the fuel pump relay is turned ON and power is supplied to the fuel pump. Also, when the engine speed drops under the set value, a control to stop the driving of the fuel pump by turning OFF the fuel pump relay is executed to take measure for a hard stop.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001S0000300ENG.html", "FUEL PRESSURE CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001S0000300ENG.html", "The ECM controls the pressure control valve with input signals from each sensor to achieve high fuel pressure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001S0000300ENG.html", "By injecting fuel at high pressure, the fuel is atomized and the combustibility is improved. This improves fuel economy.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001S0000300ENG.html", "System Configuration", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001S0000300ENG.html", "ECM calculates the target fuel pressure in accordance with the engine speed and the fuel injection amount. To this value, the following compensations are made to calculate the target fuel pressure that is suitable for the driving conditions. Then, the ECM compares the target fuel pressure with the actual fuel pressure, and actuates the pressure control valve so that the actual fuel pressure will attain the target fuel pressure (feedback control). Fuel economy is improved by adjusting the fuel pressure optimally. Also, by driving the fuel pump (high pressure) only when the fuel pressure needs to be adjusted, the driving torque of the camshaft is reduced (friction reduction).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001T0000500ENG.html", "LINEAR A/F SENSOR HEATER AND OXYGEN SENSOR (REAR) HEATER CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001T0000500ENG.html", "The linear A/F sensor and the oxygen sensor (rear) respond slowly when the exhaust gas temperature is low. Therefore, the sensor responsiveness is improved by applying the electrical current to the heater to heat sensors within the exhaust gas low temperature range, such as immediately after the engine is started with low exhaust gas temperature, or while the warm-up is being performed, and when the fuel is cut at the deceleration. In accordance with the operating conditions or activation conditions of the linear A/F sensor and the oxygen sensor (rear), the ECM changes the duty ratio of the heater. The control is performed so that the linear A/F sensor and the oxygen sensor (rear) can be activated more quickly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500200000300ENG.html", "PURGE CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500200000300ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Evaporative Emission Control System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500210000200ENG.html", "EXHAUST GAS RECIRCULATION (EGR) CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500210000200ENG.html", "Refer to Engine, Engine and Emission Control, Emission Control, Description, Exhaust Gas Recirculation System .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500230000200ENG.html", "EVAPORATIVE EMISSION CONTROL SYSTEM INCORRECT PURGE FLOW MONITOR &lt;VEHICLES FOR TAIWAN>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500230000200ENG.html", "The ECM detects whether the fuel vapor leakage exists or not from the evaporative emission control system. By the specified pattern within the certain operation range, the ECM drives the purge control solenoid valve and the ventilation solenoid valve. This allows slight vacuum to be produced in the fuel tank.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500230000200ENG.html", "The ECM measures the vacuum condition through the fuel tank pressure sensor signal. By comparing the normal (expected) value and the actual value, the ECM detects whether the fuel vapor leakage exists or not from the evaporative emission control system.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "AUTO STOP & GO (AS&G) CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The purpose of the Auto Stop & Go (AS&G) system is to reduce CO2 exhaust gases from vehicles. The AS&G system automatically should stop the engine when the vehicle is stopped. And also the system should automatically restart the engine when the vehicle is started. The ECM judges whether the engine should be stopped or restarted. The ECM also stops or restarts the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The ECM monitors the vehicle condition by using the signals from sensors and each ECU. If the specified conditions are satisfied, the ECM should stop the engine (auto stop). As for the auto stop, the coast stop function, which stops the engine not only when the vehicle is stopped but also when the vehicle is being decelerated to 22 km/h or less, is available. When the driver tries to start the vehicle, the ECM should swiftly restart the engine (auto start). As for the auto start of vehicles with 48V Mild Hybrid system, the belt drive starter generator (BSG) starts the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "SYSTEM CONFIGURATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "1. Auto Stop & Go (AS&G) System", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "When the ignition switch is turned ON or when the engine starts, the AS&G system should automatically be turned ON. The driver can turn OFF the AS&G system by pressing the AS&G OFF switch. At that time, the AS&G OFF symbol will be displayed in the combination meter. When the AS&G OFF switch is pressed again, the AS&G system should be turned ON.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "After the ignition switch is turned ON, the AS&G OFF symbol will be displayed for a few seconds.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "2. Auto Stop Control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Auto stop when the vehicle is stopped", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "While the AS&G mode is ON (AS&G OFF symbol is not displayed), if the auto stop when the vehicle is stopped is possible during driving, the AS&G symbol will be displayed in the combination meter.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "&lt;Auto stop possible condition when the vehicle is stopped>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The driver\'s seat belt is fastened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The driver\'s door is closed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine hood is closed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The shift lever is in the D range.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle has been driven in the D range after the engine start.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "At least 30 seconds have passed since the engine was started.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "At least 10 seconds have passed after the auto start.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature is 39°C or more.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The auto stop is permitted by the A/C.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle consumption current is less than or equal to the specified value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The 12V battery is in good condition (The battery is not deteriorated and the SOC is specified value or more).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The hill descent control is deactivated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The key is in the vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The cut-off plug is not removed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine warning light (check indicator light) is OFF.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The CVT warning light is OFF.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The AS&G-related device is not defective.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The auto stop is permitted by the 48V mild hybrid.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The ECM will stop the engine by performing fuel cut and full-closing control of the throttle valve when the following operation is performed while the AS&G symbol is displayed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Depress the brake pedal when the vehicle is running to stop the vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Depress the brake pedal continuously when the vehicle has completely stopped (The vehicle is determined to be stopped when the brake master cylinder fluid pressure is more than or equal to the specified value).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "However, the auto stop does not work when one or more of the following conditions are satisfied.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The brake master cylinder fluid pressure is less than the specified value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The accelerator pedal is depressed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The steering wheel is being steered.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The parking brake is applied.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vacuum pressure in the brake booster is insufficient.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The inclination angle is ±10% or more.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The CVT fluid temperature is less than 18°C.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "In addition, when one or more of the following conditions are satisfied, the auto stop will be prohibited.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The AS&G function is deactivated by pressing the AS&G OFF switch (The AS&G OFF symbol is displayed).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The AS&G-related device is defective (The AS&G OFF symbol flashes).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Coast stop", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "When the AS&G symbol is displayed (the auto stop when the vehicle is stopped is possible) and all of the conditions below are satisfied, the coast stop function, which stops the engine while the vehicle is being decelerated, will be activated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "&lt;Coast stop possible conditions>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle speed is approximately 22 km/h or less.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The brake pedal is depressed (The brake master cylinder fluid pressure is more than or equal to the specified value).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The accelerator pedal is not depressed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The steering wheel is not being steered.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The parking brake is not applied.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle has been driven at 5 km/h or more.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The ASC/ABS is deactivated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle is not being abruptly decelerated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vacuum pressure in the brake booster is sufficient.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature is 60°C or more.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The estimated gradient is within ±5% (The first time: within ±1%)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The FCM is deactivated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "If even one of the conditions above is not satisfied, the coast stop does not work even when the AS&G symbol is displayed (The auto stop when the vehicle is stopped can be performed).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "3. Auto Start Control", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "If the following motions are carried out during the auto stop even one time, the ECM displays the AS&G OFF symbol in the combination meter and prohibits the auto start.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Even if trying to return to the previous status after that, the auto start should be prohibited. When restarted, the engine must be started by the key/engine switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "At this time, the engine is started by the starter motor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "In case the hood is opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "When in the states mentioned above, the ECM should send the signal to the combination meter via the CAN to sound the warning buzzer built into the combination meter. In addition, a message \"Auto Stop & Go Not Available\" will be displayed on the information display. This warns the driver that this is different from normal use.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "When the ECM fails to perform auto start, the AS&G OFF symbol will be displayed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Normal Auto Start", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "If the brake pedal is released during the auto stop, the ECM drives the belt drive starter generator, starts the engine immediately and hides the AS&G symbol.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The auto start will also be activated when any of the following operations is performed in the state between when the coast stop is activated and when the vehicle is stopped.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Depress the accelerator pedal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Shift the selector lever to the range other than the D range.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "Forcible Auto Start", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "When any of the following conditions is satisfied during the auto stop (when the vehicle is stopped), the ECM starts the engine swiftly despite the driver\'s determination.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The driver\'s seat belt is not fastened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The driver\'s door is opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature is 32°C or less.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "3 minutes have passed after auto stop.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle consumption current is more than or equal to the specified value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The 12V battery is insufficiently charged.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The vehicle speed is not 0 km/h.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The auto start request is received from the A/C.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The hill descent control switch is ON.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The key is outside the vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The AS&G OFF switch is ON.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The AS&G-related device is defective.*", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The auto start request is received from the 48V mild hybrid.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "*: The AS&G OFF symbol flashes at this time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "In addition, when any of the following conditions is satisfied in the state between when the coast stop is activated and when the vehicle is stopped, the ECM starts the engine swiftly despite the driver\'s determination.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "An increase in vehicle speed is detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The estimated gradient is ±5% or more.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001X0000801ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature is 53°C or less.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001Y0000200ENG.html", "BELT DRIVE STARTER GENERATOR (BSG) CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001Y0000200ENG.html", "Refer to ELECTRIC POWER TRAIN - 48V mild hybrid, Description, General Information .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "WATER FLOW CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "The ECM supplies current to the motor which is incorporated into the multi flow control valve to rotate the internal rotary valve to open/close each path (radiator path, EGR cooler and heater path, engine oil cooler and CVT warmer path) and distributes the engine coolant flow rate.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "When the engine coolant temperature is low, the ECM closes all the paths to promote engine warm-up.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "By opening/closing the valve according to the state of the parts on the engine coolant path, unnecessary energy consumption is reduced and fuel efficiency is improved.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Multi flow control valve operation pattern", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Engine coolant path", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Operation pattern during warm-up", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Operation pattern after warm-up", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "(1) Radiator", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Close", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Close ↔ Open", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "(2) EGR cooler and heater", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "Open", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001U0000200ENG.html", "(3) Engine oil cooler and CVT warmer", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012X0000200ENG.html", "ENGINE OIL PRESSURE CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012X0000200ENG.html", "The engine oil pump with the rotor mechanism, which can vary the engine oil pump capacity by the oil relief control valve, has been adopted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012X0000200ENG.html", "According to the driving conditions, the ECM controls the driving of the oil relief control valve to adjust the discharge amount of the oil pump so that the hydraulic pressure becomes the set target hydraulic pressure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012X0000200ENG.html", "This optimizes the drive torque of the oil pump, thus reducing engine output loss.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012X0000200ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001V0000300ENG.html", "ELECTRIC WATER PUMP CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001V0000300ENG.html", "The water-cooled intercooler has a different cooling path from that for the engine coolant and the coolant is circulated by the electric water pump.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001V0000300ENG.html", "The ECM controls the intake air temperature to an appropriate temperature by changing the rotation speed of the electric water pump by the PWM (Pulse Wide Modulation) according to the driving conditions", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001V0000300ENG.html", "In addition, the ECM monitors the rotation speed to check if the target rotation speed is obtained according to the actual rotation speed signal (PWM) from the electric water pump.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001V0000300ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012Z0000700ENG.html", "48V BATTERY FAN & MOTOR CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012Z0000700ENG.html", "The ECM controls the rotation speed of the 48V battery fan & motor by the PWM (Pulse Wide Modulation).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012Z0000700ENG.html", "The ECM optimally controls the rotation speed of the fan according to the temperature of the 48V battery module and the 48V DC-DC converter and changes the rotation speed of the fan according to the vehicle speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012Z0000700ENG.html", "In addition, the ECM monitors the rotation speed to check if the target rotation speed is obtained according to the actual rotation speed signal from the 48V battery fan & motor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012Z0000700ENG.html", "System Configuration Diagram", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "CRUISE CONTROL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SYSTEM DIAGRAM", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Component parts", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Function", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Stoplight switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cruise control switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "TCM", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "It transmits the output shaft speed signal to ECM via CAN communication.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "It transmits the park/neutral position signal to ECM via CAN communication.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Combination meter", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "It transmits the vehicle speed signal to ECM via CAN communication.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "It receives the cruise control status signal from ECM via CAN communication.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "ECM", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Throttle valve control servo", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SWITCHES AND INDICATORS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cruise indicator", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "CANCEL switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "RES+ switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SET- switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cruise ON/OFF switch", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "On the combination meter", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "On the steering wheel", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SET SPEED RANGE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cruise control system can be set the following vehicle speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Minimum speed (Approx.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Maximum speed (Approx.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "30 km/h", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "135 km/h", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SWITCH OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cancels the cruise control driving.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Resumes the set speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Increases speed incrementally during cruise control driving.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Sets desired cruise speed when there is no set speed", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Sets desired cruise speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Decreases speed incrementally during cruise control driving.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Master switch to activate the cruise control system.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "BASIC CRUISE CONTROL SYSTEM", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Refer to Owner\'s Manual for cruise control operating instructions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Cruise control system allows a driver to keep vehicle at predetermined constant speed without depressing accelerator pedal. Driver can set vehicle speed in advance between approximately 30 km/h and 135 km/h.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "ECM controls throttle angle of throttle valve control servo to regulate engine speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "The cruise control operation status is indicated by two indicators (CRUISE and SET on the information display) on the combination meter. If any malfunction occurs in cruise control system, SET indicator blinks and cruise control is deactivated.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Always drive vehicle in safe manner according to traffic conditions and obey all traffic laws.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "SET OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Press cruise ON/OFF switch. (CRUISE is indicated on the information display.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When vehicle speed reaches a desired speed between approximately 30 km/h and 135 km/h, press SET- switch or RES+ switch. (Then SET is indicated on the information display.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "If press RES+ switch when there is no set speed, the set speed is set to the current speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "ACCELERATE OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "If the RES+ switch is pressed during cruise control driving, increase the vehicle speed until the switch is released or vehicle speed reaches maximum speed controlled by the system.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "And then cruise control system will keep the new set speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "CANCEL OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When any of following conditions exist, cruise operation will be canceled.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "CANCEL switch is pressed", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "More than 2 switches at cruise control switch are pressed at the same time (Set speed will be cleared)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Brake pedal is depressed", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Selector lever is changed to N, P, R position", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Vehicle speed decreased to 13 km/h lower than the set speed", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Traction control system is operated", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When the ECM detects any of the following conditions, the ECM will cancel the cruise operation and inform the driver by blinking indicators.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Engine coolant temperature is slightly higher than the normal operating temperature, CRUISE indicator may blink slowly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When the engine coolant temperature decreases to the normal operating temperature, CRUISE indicator will stop blinking and the cruise operation will be able to work by pressing SET- switch or RES+ switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Malfunction for some self-diagnoses regarding cruise control: SET indicator will blink quickly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "If cruise ON/OFF switch is turned to OFF during cruise control system is activated, all of cruise control system operations will be canceled and vehicle speed memory will be erased.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "COAST OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When the SET- switch is pressed during cruise control driving, decrease vehicle set speed until the switch is released. And then cruise control system will keep the new set speed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "RESUME OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "When the RES+ switch is pressed after cancel operation other than pressing cruise ON/OFF switch is performed, vehicle speed will return to last set speed. To resume vehicle set speed, vehicle condition must meet following conditions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025001W0000201ENG.html", "Brake pedal is released", "ptxt");
