si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "TROUBLESHOOTING STRATEGY", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If a diagnosis code is erased, its \"freeze frame\" data will also be erased and system readiness test status will be stored again. Store the \"freeze frame\" data before erasing the diagnosis code.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Use these steps to plan your diagnostic strategy. If you follow them carefully, you will be sure to have exhausted most of the possible ways to find an DI and MPI fault.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Gather as much information as possible about the complaint from the customer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Verify that the condition described by the customer exists.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Check the vehicle for any DI and MPI Diagnosis Code.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If you cannot verify the condition and there are no diagnosis codes, the malfunction is intermittent. For information on how to cope with intermittent malfunctions, refer to GENERAL INFORMATION - General Information - Basic Inspection - Service information for Electrical Incident - .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If you can verify the condition but there are no diagnosis codes, or the system cannot communicate with the scan tool, refer to the trouble symptom classification table .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If there is a diagnosis code, store the number of the code, then erase the code from the memory using the scan tool.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Reconfirm the malfunction symptom and carry out a test drive with the drive cycle pattern.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If diagnosis code is set again, carry out an inspection with appropriate diagnostic code procedures.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "If diagnosis code is not set again, the malfunction is intermittent. For information on how to cope with intermittent malfunctions, refer to GENERAL INFORMATION - General Information - Basic Inspection - Service information for Electrical Incident - .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "After repairs are completed, conduct a road test duplicating the complaint set conditions to confirm the malfunction has been corrected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "Erase the permanent diagnosis code. Refer to Diagnostic Function - Permanent diagnosis code for the procedures of erasing the permanent diagnosis code .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049A0000300ENG.html", "This is carried out to prevent the failure to pass the Inspection and Maintenance (I/M) test in the states checking whether the permanent diagnosis code is set or not.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "MALFUNCTION INDICATOR LIGHT (SERVICE ENGINE SOON OR CHECK ENGINE LIGHT)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "When the abnormal condition occurs with respect to the items of Direct Fuel Injection and Multipoint Fuel Injection (DFI and MPI) system shown in the table, the engine warning light will illuminate or flash. When the light remains illuminated after the engine start, or when the light is illuminated while the engine is running, check the diagnosis code output. When the engine warning light-related circuit is normal, the engine warning light will illuminate as a bulb check by turning on the ignition switch and then go out after the engine starts.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "Items Indicated by the Malfunction Indicator Light (SERVICE ENGINE SOON or Check Engine Light)", "title");
