si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "After the ECM has detected a malfunction, the engine warning light illuminates when the engine is next turned on and the same malfunction is re-detected. However, for items marked with a \"*1\" in the diagnosis code number column, the engine warning light illuminates only on the first detection of the malfunction.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "The codes marked with a \"*2\" in the diagnosis code number column have the following two conditions for illuminating the engine warning light.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "In case that the misfire causing the damaged catalyst is detected, the engine warning light will flash until the condition is corrected. If the system detects the same malfunction after the next engine start and then the condition is corrected, the engine warning light will illuminate.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "In case that the misfire deteriorating the exhaust gas is detected, the engine warning light is illuminated when the same malfunction is redetected after the next engine start.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "Even if the malfunction is not detected when the ECM monitors the malfunction three consecutive times* after the engine warning light illuminates, turn off the engine warning light when the engine starts next time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003S0000I00ENG.html", "*: In this case, \"one time\" in monitoring the malfunction means the period from the time of the current engine start to the time of the next engine start. \"one time\" in monitoring the misfire or the fuel system malfunction means the time when the operating conditions (such as the engine speed or the engine coolant temperature) becomes similar operating conditions of the first detected malfunction.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012W0000A00ENG.html", "CHARGE WARNING LIGHT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012W0000A00ENG.html", "48V MILD HYBRID system supplies the electric power to the 12V components and charges the 12V battery through the DC-DC converter. The charge warning light turns on when electric power supply to the 12V components stops. Normally, the charge warning light turns on only while the engine is stopped (except during Auto stop). The charge warning light also turns on when an abnormality occurs in the components of the 48V MILD HYBRID system. In this case, check whether the diagnosis code is set in the ECM. The diagnosis codes for which the charge warning light turns on are shown in the table below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025012W0000A00ENG.html", "CHARGE WARNING LIGHT INSPECTION ITEMS", "title");
