si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003V0000B00ENG.html", "When detecting a malfunction, the ECM should store it. When detecting the same malfunction again after the next engine start, the ECM should blink the AS&G OFF display screen because the ECM judges the malfunction surely occurs.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "INSPECTION WITH M.U.T.-III SE DATA LIST AND ACTUATOR TEST", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "Reading data list or performing an actuator test using M.U.T.-III SE enables you to check the vehicle body harnesses and components for abnormalities. Sensor input or output to the actuator can be displayed in numerical values or graphs in the data list while in the actuator test the actuator can be forced to drive (ON/OFF driving in the specified time).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "DIAGNOSIS PROCEDURE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "Connect M.U.T.-III SE to perform inspection with the data list and actuator test function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "If any abnormality is found, inspect and repair vehicle body harnesses and components.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "After repair, check that input and output have returned to normal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "If a failure code which is caused by inspection and repair work is generated, erase the failure code.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003X0000800ENG.html", "Disconnect M.U.T.-III SE and perform a test run to check that the malfunction phenomenon is resolved.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502501610000700ENG.html", "1ST TRIP DTC (PROVISIONAL DTC)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502501610000700ENG.html", "The Diagnosis Code has two types of code: One turns on the malfunction indicator light (SERVICE ENGINE SOON or check engine light) when a malfunction is detected for the first time, and the other stores the status to ECM when a malfunction is detected for the first time, and it judges that the malfunction occurs surely when the same malfunction is detected during the next driving after the power unit is started, and turns on the malfunction indicator light (SERVICE ENGINE SOON or check engine light).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502501610000700ENG.html", "Regarding the diagnosis code which turns on the malfunction indicator light (SERVICE ENGINE SOON or check engine light) when a malfunction is detected for second time, the diagnosis code stored in the ECM when the malfunction is detected for the first time is called 1st trip DTC. When the diagnosis code is read using the M.U.T.-III SE, the \"1t\" is displayed on the set diagnosis code so that whether it is 1st trip DTC or not can be determined.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502501610000700ENG.html", "For how to read and delete the 1st trip DTC, refer to Method of Reading and Erasing Diagnostic Codes ).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "PERMANENT DIAGNOSIS CODE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "The permanent diagnosis code (PDiagnosis Code) is set in the EEPROM of the ECM as the permanent status, which checks that the malfunction of the emission related components/the system has not been repaired yet. When detecting the malfunction necessary to illuminate the engine warning light (Check Engine light), the ECM illuminates the MIL and sets the appropriate diagnosis code as the Pdiagnosis code in the EEPROM concurrently. The ECM can store up to 6 PDiagnosis Codes. The ECM, therefore, cannot store the 7th and subsequent PDiagnosis Codes. If the temporary malfunction causes the engine warning light to be illuminated and then the reinstatement during the subsequent driving causes it to be extinguished, the Pdiagnosis code is erased. Also if the ECM checks that the diagnosis code malfunction is fixed during the driving after the diagnosis code repair is completed, the Pdiagnosis code is erased. The PDiagnosis Code, however, is not erased by disconnecting the battery terminal or erasing with M.U.T.-III SE. The Pdiagnosis code can be erased if all readiness status are erased or not completed at the time of reprogramming the ECM. If the vehicle is repaired, the Pdiagnosis code can be erased by the procedures shown below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "PROCEDURES FOR ERASING PERMANENT DIAGNOSIS CODE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "Check that the diagnosis code is not set. If the diagnosis code is set, perform the diagnosis code troubleshooting, then repair the diagnosis code.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "Drive the vehicle in the drive cycle pattern suitable for the permanent diagnosis code. (Refer to )", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025003Z0000800ENG.html", "Check that the permanent diagnosis code is erased. If the permanent diagnosis code is not erased, check the diagnosis code or the provisional diagnosis code. If the malfunction code is set, repair the diagnosis code. Try to erase the permanent diagnosis code again (from Step 1 to 2). If the malfunction code is not set, the drive cycle pattern (Step 2) monitoring the malfunction can possibly be insufficient.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "MODE 6 REFERENCE TABLE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "The engine control module (ECM) monitors the condition of emission control system.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "By selecting MODE 06 using scan tool, Test Result and Limit Value (minimum) *1 or (maximum)*2 about the main items of emission control system which ECM monitors can be confirmed. The value at the last monitoring is output by ECM as a test result.", "ptxt");
