si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Fuel System Monitor Bank1A/F Signal Noise Counts In Port Fuel Injection Mode&lt;Vehicles for Taiwan>", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "ECM checks the air-fuel signal noise counts in port fuel injection mode in order to monitor the air-fuel ratio cylinder imbalance.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "× 1 count", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "9A", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Fuel System Monitor Bank1A/F Signal Noise Counts In Direct Injection Mode&lt;Vehicles for Taiwan>", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "ECM checks the air-fuel signal noise counts in direct fuel injection mode in order to monitor the air-fuel ratio cylinder imbalance.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "A2", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "0B", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder1 DataEWMA Misfire Counts For Previous Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "ECM monitors angular acceleration of crankshaft and detect misfire. EWMA (Exponential Weighted Moving Average) misfire counts for previous driving cycles.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "0C", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder1 DataMisfire Counts For Last/Current Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "ECM monitors angular acceleration of crankshaft and detect misfire. Misfire counts for last/current driving cycles.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "A3", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder2 DataEWMA Misfire Counts For Previous Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder2 DataMisfire Counts For Last/Current Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "A4", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder3 DataEWMA Misfire Counts For Previous Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder3 DataMisfire Counts For Last/Current Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder4 DataEWMA Misfire Counts For Previous Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "Mis-Fire Cylinder4 DataMisfire Counts For Last/Current Driving Cycles", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "*1: Minimum value: The test fails if test value is less than this value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "*2: Maximum value: The test fails if test value is greater than this value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "When not finishing the monitor of the driving cycle for the request of On-Board Monitoring Test Request, the ECM outputs the stored latest monitor test result.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "When the monitored test results are erased by the battery disconnection and so on, the ECM outputs the values in hexadecimal of \"0000\" or \"FFFF\", otherwise it outputs abnormal values and so on. In case of this, the ECU outputs are handled as invalid-values. When the first monitor (Readiness Status) is completed after this, the ECM outputs the valid-values.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048X0000400ENG.html", "\"Test Limit Type & Component ID byte\" output from the ECM is given in hexadecimal of \"00\" or \"80\". \"00\" means the maximum value and \"80\" means the minimum value.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048T0000400ENG.html", "ON-BOARD DIAGNOSTICS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048T0000400ENG.html", "The engine control module (ECM) monitors the input/output signals (some signals all the time and others under specified conditions) of the ECM. When a malfunction continues for a specified time or longer after the irregular signal is initially monitored, the ECM judges that a malfunction has occurred. After the ECM first detects a malfunction, a diagnosis code is recorded when the engine is restarted and the same malfunction is re-detected. However, for items marked with a \"*\", a diagnosis code is recorded on the first detection of the malfunction. The diagnostic results can be read out with a scan tool. Since memorization of the diagnosis codes is backed up directly by the battery, the diagnostic results are memorized even if the ignition key is turned off. The diagnosis codes will, however, be erased when the battery terminal or the ECM connector is disconnected. In addition, the diagnosis code can also be erased by turning the ignition switch to ON and sending the diagnosis code erase signal from M.U.T.-III SE to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048T0000400ENG.html", "If the sensor connector is disconnected with the ignition switch turned on, the diagnosis code is memorized. In this case, send the diagnosis code erase signal to the ECM in order to erase the diagnostic memory. The diagnosis items are all indicated sequentially from the smallest code number. The ECM records the engine operating condition when the diagnosis code is set. This data is called \"Freeze-frame\" data. This data can be read by using the scan tool, and can then be used in simulation tests for troubleshooting. Data items are as follows:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048T0000400ENG.html", "If the ECM detects multiple malfunctions, the ECM stores the \"Freeze-frame\" data for only the first item that was detected. However, if the ECM detects a misfire or a fuel system malfunction, the ECM stores the data by giving priority to the misfire or fuel system malfunction, regardless of the order in which the malfunction was detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025048T0000400ENG.html", "As for Diagnosis code P1603, \"Freeze-frame\" data is not memorized.", "ptxt");
