si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "SYSTEM READINESS TEST STATUS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "PURPOSE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "The Readiness function (also referred to as I/M Readiness or I/M Flags) indicates if a full diagnostic check has been \"Completed\" (is \"Ready\") for each non-continuous monitor. Enhanced I/M State Emission Programs will use the Readiness status (Codes) to see if the vehicle is ready for OBD-II testing. \"Incomplete\" (Not Ready) codes will be one of the triggers for I/M failure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "OVERVIEW", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "The ECM monitors the following main diagnosis items and records whether the evaluation was completed or is incomplete. The Readiness Codes are established for the I/M programs, thereby confirming that the vehicles have not been tampered with by erasing the diagnosis code(s) (Diagnosis Codes) before I/M testing. The Readiness Codes and diagnosis codes can be set again by disconnecting the battery or by erasing the codes with a scan tool (M.U.T.-IIISE). For this reason, all the Readiness Codes must be displayed \"Complete\" before I/M testing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "When the monitors run and complete, the scan tool (M.U.T.-IIISE) will display the Readiness Codes as \"Complete\" (General Scan Tools display as \"Ready\"). When the vehicle is operating normally and the OBD-II Drive Cycle is carried out, the Readiness Codes will be generated as \"Complete\" on the first drive cycle. For diagnosis codes requiring two drive cycles to detect a fault, the second drive cycle is required to generate the Readiness Codes as \"Complete\" if a fault is detected during the first drive cycle. If the fault is still there after the second drive cycle, a diagnosis code will be set.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "&lt;Vehicles for Taiwan>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Catalyst: P0421-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "EGR and/or VVT system: P0011-00, P0012-00, P0014-00, P0015-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Evaporative emission system: P0455-00, P0456-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Oxygen sensor (rear): P0139-00, P0140-00, P013E-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Oxygen sensor (rear) heater: P0054-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Linear A/F sensor: P0133-00, P014C-00, P014D-00, P015A-00, P015B-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Linear A/F sensor heater: P0053-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "&lt;Vehicles for Vietnam>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Oxygen sensor (rear): P0139-00, P013E-00 , P0140-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Oxygen sensor (rear) heater: P0037-00, P0038-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Linear A/F sensor: P0133-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "Linear A/F sensor (rear) heater: P0031-00, P0032-00", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "After all the Readiness Codes are displayed as \"Complete\", the technician is assured that any diagnosis codes related to the monitor will be displayed if the system has a problem. That is why some State\'s I/M programs require the Readiness Code as \"Complete\" before they check for diagnosis codes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025049B0000500ENG.html", "After a repair is made for a diagnosis code, the technician should drive the OBD-II Drive Cycle checking that the scan tool (M.U.T.-IIISE) displays all the Readiness Codes as \"Complete\".", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500420000E00ENG.html", "FAIL-SAFE FUNCTION REFERENCE TABLE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500420000E00ENG.html", "The control is carried out, which keeps the safety driving by the preset control logic when the diagnosis code is set. The diagnosis code having the fail-safe function is as follows.", "ptxt");
