si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "Code No. P0095-00: Air Temperature Sensor circuit offset (throttle intake) &lt;Vehicles for Taiwan>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "CIRCUIT OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "A power voltage of 5 V is applied to the No. 2 intake air temperature sensor power terminal of boost pressure sensor from the ECM connector terminal UATS.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "The power voltage is grounded to the ECM connector terminal MAPE from the No. 2 intake air temperature sensor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "TECHNICAL DESCRIPTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "The No. 2 intake air temperature sensor converts the intake air temperature into a voltage and inputs the voltage signal to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "In response to the signal, the ECM corrects the fuel injection amount, etc.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "The No. 2 intake air temperature sensor is a kind of resistor, which has characteristics to reduce its resistance as the intake air temperature rises. Therefore, the sensor output voltage varies with the intake air temperature, and becomes lower as the intake air temperature rises.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "DESCRIPTIONS OF MONITOR METHODS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "The temperature change of No. 2 intake air temperature sensor is too small or too large relative to the temperature change of the other temperature sensors (engine coolant temperature sensor, No. 1 intake air temperature sensor, No. 3 intake air temperature sensor, EGR gas temperature sensor).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025004S0000800ENG.html", "MONITOR EXECUTION", "title");
