si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "Code No. P011B-00: Engine coolant temperature offset &lt;Vehicles for Taiwan>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "CIRCUIT OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "A power voltage of 5 V is applied to the engine coolant temperature sensor power terminal from the ECM connector terminal WTS.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "The power voltage is grounded to the ECM connector terminal WTSE from the engine coolant temperature sensor.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "TECHNICAL DESCRIPTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature sensor converts the engine coolant temperature into a voltage signal, and inputs the voltage to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "In response to the signal, the ECM controls the fuel injection amount and the fast idle speed when the engine is cold state.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "The engine coolant temperature sensor is a kind of resistor, which has characteristics to reduce its resistance as the engine coolant temperature rises. Therefore, the sensor output voltage varies with the engine coolant temperature, and becomes lower as the engine coolant temperature rises.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "DESCRIPTIONS OF MONITOR METHODS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025005G0000500ENG.html", "The temperature change of engine coolant temperature sensor is too small or too large relative to the temperature change of the other temperature sensors (No. 1 intake air temperature sensor, No. 2 intake air temperature sensor, No. 3 intake air temperature sensor, EGR gas temperature sensor).", "ptxt");
