si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "Code No. P040C-00: Exhaust Gas Recirculation Temperature Sensor Circuit Low", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "CIRCUIT OPERATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "A power voltage of 5 V is applied to the EGR gas temperature sensor output terminal from the ECM connector terminal EGRT.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "The power voltage is grounded to the ECM connector terminal ETSE from the EGR gas temperature sensor connector terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "TECHNICAL DESCRIPTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "The EGR gas temperature sensor converts the EGR temperature into a voltage and inputs the voltage signal to the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "The EGR gas temperature sensor is a kind of resistor, which has characteristics to reduce its resistance as the EGR gas temperature rises. Therefore, the sensor output voltage varies with the EGR gas temperature, and becomes lower as the EGR gas temperature rises.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "DESCRIPTIONS OF MONITOR METHODS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502500790000500ENG.html", "The EGR gas temperature sensor is a kind of resistor that features a reduction in resistance when the exhaust gas temperature rises. Therefore, the sensor output voltage changes according to the exhaust gas temperature. When exhaust gas temperature rises, it lowers.", "ptxt");
