si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "The ECM terminal FPR5 supplies a 5 volts reference signal to the fuel tank pressure sensor. The fuel tank pressure sensor is grounded through the ECM terminal FPRE.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "The fuel tank pressure sensor returns a voltage signal to the ECM terminal F/PR that is proportional to the pressure in the fuel tank.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "TECHNICAL DESCRIPTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "To determine whether the fuel tank pressure sensor is defective, the ECM monitors the fuel tank pressure sensor output voltage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "The ECM judges if the fuel tank pressure sensor output voltage is normal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025007I0000400ENG.html", "In rare cases, this diagnosis code may be also set under some fuel and driving conditions regardless of the fuel pressure sensor output voltage when the fuel system is clogged.", "ptxt");
