si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "When removing the fuel pipe, etc., release fuel pressure to prevent fuel spray.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "&lt;Low pressure side>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Remove the second seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior – Seat – Second Seat Assembly – &lt;Vehicles for 7 Persons>, &lt;Vehicles for 5 Persons>) and turn up the floor carpet.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Remove the inspection hole cover (RH).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Using a screwdriver, remove it by turning clips clockwise by 90 degrees.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Disconnect the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Crank the engine for at least two seconds.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "If the engine is not started, turn the ignition switch to the OFF position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "If the engine is started, turn the ignition switch to the OFF position after the engine stopped.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Connect the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Install the inspection hole cover (RH).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Return the floor carpet to the original condition and install the second seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior – Seat – Second Seat Assembly – &lt;Vehicles for 7 Persons>, &lt;Vehicles for 5 Persons>).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "&lt;High pressure side>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "To prevent damage to the M.U.T.-III SE always turn the ignition switch to the OFF position before connecting or disconnecting the M.U.T.-III SE.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Connect the M.U.T.-III SE to the diagnosis connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Start the engine and run at idle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Check \"Item No. A2301: Fuel pressure\" from the M.U.T.-III SE data list.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "When the data list item A2301 reaches approximately 10,000 kPa, turn the ignition switch to OFF position and wait until the engine is cool.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Disconnect the M.U.T.-III SE.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Cover the hose connection with rags to prevent splash of fuel that could be caused by some residual pressure in the fuel pipe line.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Cover the connection between the fuel pump (high pressure) and fuel delivery intermediate pipe with a waste cloth.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002G0000500ENG.html", "Loosen the fuel delivery intermediate pipe at the fuel pump (high pressure).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "FUEL PUMP OPERATION CHECK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Open the fuel filler door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Using M.U.T.-III SE, forcibly drive the fuel pump (integrated in the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly) to check the fuel pump operation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "The operating sound of the fuel pump is difficult to be heard because the pump is in-tank type. Therefore, open the flap of the capless unit at the fuel filler neck part by inserting a bar or a nozzle with diameter of Φ20 - 21 mm (0.79 - 0.82 inches) to check the sound from the fuel filler port.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Close the fuel filler door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "If the fuel pump does not operate, follow the procedure below to check the pump for operation. If it is normal, check the driving circuit.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Turn the ignition switch to the OFF position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Remove the second seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior – Seat – Second Seat Assembly – &lt;Vehicles for 7 Persons>, &lt;Vehicles for 5 Persons>) and turn up the floor carpet.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Remove the Inspection hole cover (RH).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Disconnect the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "When the battery is connected to the connector terminals No. 3 and 6 (fuel tank pump and gauge assembly side), check that the pump operating sound can be heard. When the pump operating sound cannot be heard, replace the fuel pump (Refer to Engine &lt;4B4> – Fuel Supply – On-vehicle Service – ).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Check for fuel pressure by pinching the fuel hose with fingertips.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Connect the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Install the Inspection hole cover (RH).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5025002H0000500ENG.html", "Return the floor carpet to the original condition and install the rear seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior – Seat – Second Seat Assembly – &lt;Vehicles for 7 Persons>, &lt;Vehicles for 5 Persons>).", "ptxt");
