si[i++] = gsitm("N502430030000U00ENG.html", "&lt;4WD>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430030000U00ENG.html", "This fuel system is designed with consideration for global environment protection to ensure safety at a collision, reduce weight, and improve reliability and quality. This system has the following features:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430030000U00ENG.html", "A quick-joint connector of a plastic tube is used for the fuel high-pressure hose in the engine compartment to reduce the permeation of fuel evaporative emission.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430030000U00ENG.html", "The surface of under floor fuel line pipes is coated with 1 mm thickness of resin to improve resistance to corrosion and chipping.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430030000U00ENG.html", "The sealed type fuel tank assembly has been adopted to reduce the emission of transpiration gas in the tank.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "FUEL TANK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "The fuel tank assembly consists of components such as a fuel tank pump and gauge assembly, a fuel level sensor, and a fuel tank, and has the following features:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "The fuel tank is mounted underneath the second seats to improve safety at a collision.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "The fuel tank itself is made of a pre-coat galvanized steel sheet that contains no lead.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "The capacity of the fuel tank is approximately 55 L.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "The fuel tank pump and gauge assembly consist of the following components:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "Fuel pump", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "Fuel level sensor", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "Fuel filter", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "Fuel pressure regulator", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "CONSTRUCTION DIAGRAM", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "&lt;2WD>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430040000U00ENG.html", "&lt;4WD>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "FUEL PUMP (HIGH PRESSURE)", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "SYSTEM CONFIGURATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "The fuel pump (high pressure) sends fuel that was sucked up from the fuel tank by the fuel pump to the delivery pipe  (high pressure) with the pressure of the fuel raised up to 30 MPa. The functions of each section are as follows:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "Pressure control valve: Adjusts the amount of fuel sent to the delivery pipe  (high pressure) with the drive signal from the ECM.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "Plunger: Pressurizes the fuel stored in the chamber.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "Delivery valve: Prevents the fuel in the delivery pipe  (high pressure) from flowing back to the fuel pump (high pressure) side.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "Relief valve: Opens when the fuel pressure in the delivery pipe  (high pressure) exceeds the predetermined value to keep it at the proper pressure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "DESCRIPTION OF CONSTRUCTION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "The drive force of the fuel pump (high pressure) is transmitted from the pump cam of the exhaust camshaft to the plunger via the tappet.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "When the exhaust camshaft rotates, the plunger is driven to pressurize the fuel stored in the chamber.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "In the intake process, fuel sent from the fuel pump is drawn into the chamber. In the pressure feed process, the exhaust camshaft rotates with the pressure control valve closed, and the fuel in the chamber is pressurized. When the fuel pressure in the delivery pipe  (high pressure) is exceeded, the delivery valve opens and the fuel is forcibly fed to the delivery pipe  (high pressure). The plunger repeats the intake and pressure feed process four times for each revolution of the exhaust camshaft.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "As a result, when the fuel injector is injecting four times, the fuel pump (high pressure) is also forcibly feeding four times. Therefore, the fuel pressure in the delivery pipe  (high pressure) can be kept constant.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "PRESSURE CONTROL VALVE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "The pressure control valve is attached to the fuel passage between the fuel inlet and the chamber. The pressure control valve is a solenoid valve that closes the valve according to the drive current, and adjusts the amount of fuel pressurized in the chamber.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502430050000300ENG.html", "When the coil is not energized, the solenoid valve is open, and when the plunger is pushed up at this time, the fuel in the chamber is returned to the fuel pump side. When the coil is energized, the solenoid valve closes, and when the plunger is pushed up at this time, the fuel in the chamber is pressurized. The ECM controls the amount of fuel pressurized in the chamber by changing the drive current of the solenoid valve according to the lift amount of the pump cam.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "SERVICE SPECIFICATION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "Item", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "Standard value", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "Fuel tank temperature sensor resistance kΩ", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "at 20°C", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "2.3 - 2.7", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "at 50°C", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431010000400ENG.html", "0.79 - 0.90", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "SPECIAL TOOL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "When you order special service tool, use part number on “tool order number” of special service tool number substitution list. Refer to", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Tool", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Number", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Name", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Use", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "KV101207S0", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Unified fuel lock ring wrench", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431020000O00ENG.html", "Removing and installing lock ring", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "FUEL LEAK CHECK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "If the fuel pump (high pressure) is replaced or removed and installed, activate the fuel pump in the fuel tank before starting the engine to fill the fuel pump (high pressure) with fuel to prevent damage to the fuel pump (high pressure).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "If the fuel pump (high pressure) is replaced or removed and installed, activate the fuel pump in the fuel tank according to the steps below to fill the fuel pump (high pressure) with fuel.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Do not start the engine until the operation is finished.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Turn the ignition switch to the ON position. After 2 seconds have passed, turn the ignition switch to the OFF position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Repeat the operations above 4 times.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Start the engine to operate the fuel pump.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Turn OFF the ignition switch and stop the engine.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Perform a visual inspection to see if fuel is leaking from the fuel tank, hoses, pipes, fuel injectors, etc. (Refer to ).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Visually inspect the fuel hoses and pipes to make sure they are not cracked or broken.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Inspect each hose and pipe clamp installation to make sure they are not loose.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431090000Q00ENG.html", "Visually inspect the hose and pipe securements to make sure there are no abnormalities due to deterioration of the rubber in the clamps, etc.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431100000Q00ENG.html", "FUEL PUMP OPERATION CHECK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431100000Q00ENG.html", "Refer to Engine – DI and MPI – On-vehicle Service – .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431110000O00ENG.html", "FUEL LEVEL SENSOR CHECK", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431110000O00ENG.html", "Refer to Driver Information & Multimedia – Meter, Warning Lamp Indicator – Full TFT Meter – Diagnosis Code/Circuit Diagnosis – Fuel Level Sensor Signal Circuit .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "FUEL TANK PUMP AND GAUGE ASSEMBLY REPLACEMENT", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "&lt;2WD>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Release the fuel pressure in the fuel line (Refer to Engine - DI and MPI - On-Vehicle service - ).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Disconnect fuel main pipe quick connector according to the following instructions:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Push in the retainer (orange, white) of the fuel main pipe connector and unlock the connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Disconnect the fuel main pipe from the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Remove crossmember assembly (Refer to Body Exterior, Doors, Roof and Vehicle Security - Door and Lock - Removal and Installation - Crossmember Assembly ) &lt;Vehicles for 5 persons>.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Remove lock ring according to the following instructions.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install pawl (B) of special tool unified fuel lock ring wrench (KV101207S0) (A) to the position shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Temporarily tighten mounting bolt (B) of the pawl according to the measurement (R) from the center of special tool (KV101207S0) (A) to the end of pawl (C).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Set special tool (KV101207S0) to lock ring and tighten the mounting bolt of the pawl.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Remove lock ring.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "To prevent lock ring wrench from being detached, securely hold down spinner handle by hand.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "To reduce impact caused by removal operation, use long spinner handle [handle length: 60 cm or more] and slowly turn it counterclockwise.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Remove the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "For disassembly and reassembly of the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly, refer to .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install new O-ring to fuel tank without any twist.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Do not reuse O-rings.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly on the fuel tank with the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly face  faced the shown in the figure against the arrow vehicle front.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", ": Vehicle front", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Never allow seal packing to drop.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Never bend float arm during installing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install lock ring for fuel tank pump and gauge assembly with special tool unified fuel lock ring wrench (KV101207S0) turning clockwise.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install lock ring horizontally.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Turn the lock ring  until it is engaged in the fuel tank side  as shown in the figure.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Connect fuel main pipe quick connector according to the following instructions:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Pull up the retainer (orange) of fuel main pipe connector to unlock before installing.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install the connector of the fuel main pipe to the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly securely and push in the retainer (orange) and lock the connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "When pushing in the retainer of the fuel main pipe connector, pay attention to avoid damage to the retainer. If the fuel main pipe is not inserted completely, the retainer cannot be inserted.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "After the installation of the fuel main pipe, slightly pull the fuel main pipe to check that it is connected securely.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Connect the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly connector.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Before installing inspection hole cover, check that the connecting part has no fuel leakage.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install inspection hole covers with the front mark (arrow) facing front of vehicle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Lock clips by turning counterclockwise.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install crossmember assembly (Refer to Body Exterior, Doors, Roof and Vehicle Security - Door and Lock - Removal and Installation - Crossmember Assembly ) &lt;Vehicles for 5 persons>.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install the second seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior - Seat - Second Seat Assembly ) &lt;Vehicles for 7 persons>.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Install the second seat assembly (Refer to Body Interior - Seat - Second Seat Assembly ) &lt;Vehicles for 5 persons>.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "&lt;4WD>", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Raise the fuel tank pump and gauge assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Never bend float arm during removal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Never pollute the inside by residue fuel. Draw out avoiding inclination by supporting with a cloth.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Never cause impacts such by dropping when handling components.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Separate fuel tube as per the following steps to remove fuel tank pump and gauge assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Disconnect harness connector .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "Pinch quick connector  square-part with your fingers, and pull out the quick connector by hand.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N502431120001D00ENG.html", "If quick connector and tube on sender unit are stuck, push several times until they move, and pull out.", "ptxt");
