si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Precautions for Removing Battery Terminal", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "With the adoption of Auto ACC function, ACC power is automatically supplied by operating the Keyless operation key or remote keyless entry or by opening/closing the driver side door. In addition, ACC power is supplied even after the ignition switch is turned to the OFF position, i.e. ACC power is supplied for a certain fixed time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "When disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, turn off the ACC power before disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, observing “How to disconnect 12V battery terminal” described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Some ECUs operate for a certain fixed time even after ignition switch is turned OFF and ignition power supply is stopped. If the battery terminal is disconnected before ECU stops, accidental DTC detection or ECU data damage may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "For vehicles with the 2-batteries, be sure to connect the main battery and the sub battery before turning ON the ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "If the ignition switch is turned ON with any one of the terminals of main battery and sub battery disconnected, then DTC may be detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "After installing the 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "The removal of 12V battery may cause a DTC detection error.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "HOW TO DISCONNECT 12V BATTERY TERMINAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Disconnect 12V battery terminal according to instruction described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Open the hood.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the OFF position with the driver side door opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Get out of the vehicle and close the driver side door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "While waiting, never operate the vehicle such as locking, opening, and closing doors. Violation of this caution results in the activation of ACC power supply according to the Auto ACC function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "Remove 12V battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040304E0001300ENG.html", "After installing 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Service Notice or Precautions for Rear Final Drive", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Use recommended gear oil only.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Recommended Oil/Lubricants", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Genuine NISSAN HYPOID FLUID·S1 GL-5 75W-80 or equivalent", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Use only genuine Mitsubishi Motors parts for electro-hydraulic coupling oil.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Check for the correct installation status prior to removal or disassembly. If matching marks are required, be certain they never interfere with the function of the parts when applied.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Overhaul should be done in a clean work area, it is preferable to work in dustproof area.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Before disassembly, using steam or white gasoline, completely remove sand and mud from the exterior of the unit, preventing them from entering into the unit during disassembly or assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Check appearance of the disassembled parts for damage, deformation, and unusual wear. Replace them with a new ones if necessary.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Gaskets, seals and O-rings should be replaced any time when the unit is disassembled.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "In principle, tighten bolts or nuts gradually in several steps working diagonally from inside to outside. If tightening sequence is specified, observe it.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Clean and flush the parts sufficiently and blow-dry them.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Be careful not to damage sliding surfaces and mating surfaces.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "When applying sealant, remove the old sealant from the mounting surface; then remove any moisture, oil, and foreign materials from the application and mounting surfaces.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Always use shop paper for cleaning the inside of components.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "Never use cotton gloves or shop rags to prevent entering of lint.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5040306Z0000C00ENG.html", "During assembly, observe the specified tightening torque, and apply new gear oil, petroleum jelly, or multi-purpose grease as specified for each vehicle, if necessary.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N504030700000B00ENG.html", "Special Service Tools", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N504030700000B00ENG.html", "When you order special service tool, use part number on “tool order number” of special service tool number substitution list. Refer to", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N504030700000B00ENG.html", "The actual shapes of TechMate tools may differ from those of special service tools illustrated here.", "ptxt");
