si[i++] = gsitm("N5070202W0000R00ENG.html", "Removal and Installation", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5070202W0000R00ENG.html", "When replacing the power steering control module, always replace it with a new one. If a power steering control module which was installed to another vehicle is installed, the engine cannot be started.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5070202W0000R00ENG.html", "The power steering control module is an integral part of the steering gear and linkage. If the replacement of the power steering control module is necessary, replace the steering gear and linkage. Refer to .", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "Precaution for Supplemental Restraint System (SRS) \"AIR BAG\" and \"SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER\"", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "The Supplemental Restraint System such as “AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER”, used along with a front seat belt, helps to reduce the risk or severity of injury to the driver and front passenger for certain types of collision.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "Information necessary to service the system safely is included in the “SRS AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT” of this Service Manual.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "Always observe the following items for preventing accidental activation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "To avoid rendering the SRS inoperative, which could increase the risk of personal injury or death in the event of a collision that would result in air bag inflation, it is recommended that all maintenance and repair be performed by an authorized Mitsubishi Motors dealer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "Improper repair, including incorrect removal and installation of the SRS, can lead to personal injury caused by unintentional activation of the system. For removal of Spiral Cable and Air Bag Module, see “SRS AIR BAG”.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "Never use electrical test equipment on any circuit related to the SRS unless instructed to in this Service Manual. SRS wiring harnesses can be identified by yellow harnesses or harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS WHEN USING POWER TOOLS (AIR OR ELECTRIC) AND HAMMERS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "When working near the Air Bag Diagnosis Sensor Unit or other Air Bag System sensors with the ignition/power switch ON or engine running, never use air or electric power tools or strike near the sensor(s) with a hammer. Heavy vibration could activate the sensor(s) and deploy the air bag(s), possibly causing serious injury.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104C0000H00ENG.html", "When using air or electric power tools or hammers, always switch the ignition/power switch OFF, disconnect the 12V battery or batteries, and wait at least 3 minutes before performing any service.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Precautions for Removing Battery Terminal", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "With the adoption of Auto ACC function, ACC power is automatically supplied by operating the Keyless operation key or remote keyless entry or by opening/closing the driver side door. In addition, ACC power is supplied even after the ignition switch is turned to the OFF position, i.e. ACC power is supplied for a certain fixed time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "When disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, turn off the ACC power before disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, observing \"How to disconnect 12V battery terminal\" described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Some ECUs operate for a certain fixed time even after ignition switch is turned OFF and ignition power supply is stopped. If the battery terminal is disconnected before ECU stops, accidental DTC detection or ECU data damage may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "For vehicles with the 2-batteries, be sure to connect the main battery and the sub battery before turning ON the ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "If the ignition switch is turned ON with any one of the terminals of main battery and sub battery disconnected, then DTC may be detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "After installing the 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "The removal of 12V battery may cause a DTC detection error.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "HOW TO DISCONNECT 12V BATTERY TERMINAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Disconnect 12V battery terminal according to instruction described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Open the hood.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the OFF position with the driver side door opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Get out of the vehicle and close the driver side door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "While waiting, never operate the vehicle such as locking, opening, and closing doors. Violation of this caution results in the activation of ACC power supply according to the Auto ACC function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "Remove 12V battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102Y0000J00ENG.html", "After installing 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Precaution for Seat Belt Service", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Before removing the seat belt assembly, turn the ignition switch OFF, disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Never use electrical test equipment for seat belt connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "After replacing or reinstalling seat belt assembly, or reconnecting seat belt connectors, check the system function. Refer to M.U.T.-III SE Function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Never use disassembled buckle or seat belt assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Replace anchor bolts if they are deformed or worn out.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Never oil tongue and buckle.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "If any component of seat belt assembly is questionable, never repair. Replace the entire seat belt assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "If webbing is cut, frayed or damaged, replace seat belt assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "When replacing seat belt assembly, use a Mitsubishi Genuine seat belt assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "AFTER A COLLISION", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "To avoid the risk of death or severe injury:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Inspect all seat belt system components including the seat belt webbing, retractors, pretensioners, buckles, anchors, and attaching hardware after any collision.", "par1");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Mitsubishi Motors recommends that all seat belt assemblies and buckles in use during a collision be replaced unless the collision was minor and all seat belt system components including the seat belt webbing, retractors, pretensioners, buckles, anchors, and attaching hardware show no damage and continue to operate properly.", "par2");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Inspect all seat belt assemblies and components including webbing, retractors, buckles, anchors and attaching hardware not in use during a collision. Replace if either damage or improper operation is noted.", "par3");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Seat belt pretensioners activate whenever an air bag deploys and cannot be reused. If an air bag deploys, always replace the seat belt assemblies and system components including webbing, retractors, buckles, anchors and attaching hardware, even if the seat belts were not in use during a collision.", "par4");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Failure to follow any of the above steps could result in serious personal injury in an accident.", "par5");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Replace any seat belt assembly (including anchor bolts) if:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "The seat belt is in use at the time of a collision (except for minor collisions and the belts, retractors and buckles show no damage and continue to operate properly).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "The seat belt is damaged in an accident (i.e. torn webbing, bent retractor or guide).", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "The seat belt attaching point is damaged in an accident. Inspect the seat belt attaching area for damage or distortion and repair as necessary before installing a new seat belt assembly.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "Anchor bolts are deformed or worn out.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080102V0000I00ENG.html", "The front seat belt assembly must be replaced even if the seat belts are not in use during the collision in which the air bags are deployed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104O0000D00ENG.html", "Seat Belt Pre-tensioner with Load Limiter", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104O0000D00ENG.html", "The seat belt with pre-tensioner is installed to the centre pillar part and the quarter panel part.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104O0000D00ENG.html", "The seat belt with pre-tensioner consists of seat belt, gas generator, etc. and automatically winds the seat belt at the time of a frontal collision to reduce the forward movement of the passenger.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104P0000E00ENG.html", "Double Pre-tensioner Seat Belt", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104P0000E00ENG.html", "The lap pre-tensioner is installed to the centre pillar part.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5080104P0000E00ENG.html", "The lap pre-tensioner consists of seat belt, gas generator, etc. and automatically winds the seat belt at the time of a frontal collision to reduce the forward movement of the passenger.", "ptxt");
