si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "Precaution for Supplemental Restraint System (SRS) \"AIR BAG\" and \"SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER\"", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "The Supplemental Restraint System such as “AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT PRE-TENSIONER”, used along with a front seat belt, helps to reduce the risk or severity of injury to the driver and front passenger for certain types of collision.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "Information necessary to service the system safely is included in the “SRS AIR BAG” and “SEAT BELT” of this Service Manual.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "Always observe the following items for preventing accidental activation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "To avoid rendering the SRS inoperative, which could increase the risk of personal injury or death in the event of a collision that would result in air bag inflation, it is recommended that all maintenance and repair be performed by an authorized Mitsubishi Motors dealer.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "Improper repair, including incorrect removal and installation of the SRS, can lead to personal injury caused by unintentional activation of the system. For removal of Spiral Cable and Air Bag Module, see “SRS AIR BAG”.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "Never use electrical test equipment on any circuit related to the SRS unless instructed to in this Service Manual. SRS wiring harnesses can be identified by yellow harnesses or harness connectors.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "PRECAUTIONS WHEN USING POWER TOOLS (AIR OR ELECTRIC) AND HAMMERS", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "When working near the Air Bag Diagnosis Sensor Unit or other Air Bag System sensors with the ignition/power switch ON or engine running, never use air or electric power tools or strike near the sensor(s) with a hammer. Heavy vibration could activate the sensor(s) and deploy the air bag(s), possibly causing serious injury.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060350000E00ENG.html", "When using air or electric power tools or hammers, always switch the ignition/power switch OFF, disconnect the 12V battery or batteries, and wait at least 3 minutes before performing any service.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Precaution Necessary for Steering Wheel Rotation After Battery Disconnect", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Comply with the following cautions to prevent any error and malfunction.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Before removing and installing any control units, first turn the ignition power source and accessory power source to the OFF, then disconnect both battery cables.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "After finishing work, confirm that all control unit connectors are connected properly, then re-connect both battery cables.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Always use M.U.T.-III SE to perform self-diagnosis as a part of each function inspection after finishing work. If a DTC is detected, perform trouble diagnosis according to self-diagnosis results.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "For vehicle with steering lock unit, if the battery is disconnected or discharged, the steering wheel will lock and cannot be turned.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "If turning the steering wheel is required with the battery disconnected or discharged, follow the operation procedure below before starting the repair operation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "OPERATION PROCEDURE", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Connect both battery cables.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Supply power using jumper cables if battery is discharged.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Open driver door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Turn the ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "(At this time, the steering lock will be released.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Turn the ignition switch to OFF position with driver door open.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Wait for 3 minutes or longer with driver door open.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Do not close driver door because the steering wheel locks when driver door is closed.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "The auto acc function is adapted to this vehicle. For this reason, even when the ignition switch is turned to OFF position, the accessory power source does not turned OFF and continues to be supplied for a certain amount of time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Disconnect both battery cables. The steering lock will remain released with both battery cables disconnected and the steering wheel can be turned.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Perform the necessary repair operation.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "When the repair work is completed, re-connect both battery cables. With the brake pedal released, turn the ignition switch from OFF position to ON position, then to LOCK position. (The steering wheel will lock when the ignition switch is turned to LOCK position.)", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060360000A00ENG.html", "Perform self-diagnosis check of all control units using M.U.T.-III SE.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Precautions for Removing Battery Terminal", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "With the adoption of Auto ACC function, ACC power is automatically supplied by operating the Keyless operation key or remote keyless entry or by opening/closing the driver side door. In addition, ACC power is supplied even after the ignition switch is turned to the OFF position, i.e. ACC power is supplied for a certain fixed time.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "When disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, turn off the ACC power before disconnecting the 12V battery terminal, observing “How to disconnect 12V battery terminal” described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Some ECUs operate for a certain fixed time even after ignition switch is turned OFF and ignition power supply is stopped. If the battery terminal is disconnected before ECU stops, accidental DTC detection or ECU data damage may occur.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "For vehicles with the 2-batteries, be sure to connect the main battery and the sub battery before turning ON the ignition switch.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "If the ignition switch is turned ON with any one of the terminals of main battery and sub battery disconnected, then DTC may be detected.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "After installing the 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "The removal of 12V battery may cause a DTC detection error.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "HOW TO DISCONNECT 12V BATTERY TERMINAL", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Disconnect 12V battery terminal according to instruction described below.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Open the hood.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the ON position.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Turn ignition switch to the OFF position with the driver side door opened.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Get out of the vehicle and close the driver side door.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Wait at least 3 minutes.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "While waiting, never operate the vehicle such as locking, opening, and closing doors. Violation of this caution results in the activation of ACC power supply according to the Auto ACC function.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "Remove 12V battery terminal.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060370000E00ENG.html", "After installing 12V battery, always check the DTC of all ECUs and erase DTC.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060390000A00ENG.html", "Precaution for Procedure without Cowl Top Cover", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N514060390000A00ENG.html", "When performing the procedure after removing cowl top cover, cover the lower end of windshield with urethane, etc to prevent damage to windshield.", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5140603A0000A00ENG.html", "Precaution for Shift By Wire", "title");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5140603A0000A00ENG.html", "To avoid the risk of minor injury or property damage:", "ptxt");
si[i++] = gsitm("N5140603A0000A00ENG.html", "If the 12-volt battery has low or no voltage, the transmission cannot be shifted. Replace the battery or repair the damaged power supply system. If towing the vehicle, follow the tow procedure. Refer to .", "par1");
